225
00:09:20,227 --> 00:09:22,463
Camping! (chuckling)

226
00:09:22,463 --> 00:09:23,697
- [Man] This way.

227
00:09:23,697 --> 00:09:25,667
- [Crow] Yeah, whatever.

228
00:09:27,000 --> 00:09:29,603
- [Tom] Tonight on Music
from Hearts of Space,

229
00:09:29,603 --> 00:09:32,607
we'll go on a cosmic joyride
with some space music

230
00:09:32,607 --> 00:09:34,942
by various bay area artists.

231
00:09:37,878 --> 00:09:38,678
But first...

232
00:09:38,678 --> 00:09:42,115
(thunder rumbling)

233
00:09:42,115 --> 00:09:43,750
- [Man] There, that's the nest.

234
00:09:43,750 --> 00:09:45,118
We'll make a fortune
with that lot.

235
00:09:45,118 --> 00:09:46,587
They're nightingale's eggs.

236
00:09:46,587 --> 00:09:48,155
- [Matt] I'll believe that
when they've hatched out.

237
00:09:48,155 --> 00:09:49,723
- [Man] Lay off, will you, Matt?

238
00:09:49,723 --> 00:09:51,458
- [Joel] Just lay off.

239
00:09:51,458 --> 00:09:52,593
- [Matt] Here.

240
00:09:58,532 --> 00:09:59,733
- [Joel] Perfect.

241
00:09:59,733 --> 00:10:01,235
- Go to the truck and
bring a ladder, Sam.

242
00:10:01,235 --> 00:10:01,968
- [Tom] I didn't get cast
in the Lorne Greene role

243
00:10:01,968 --> 00:10:02,803
for nothin'.

244
00:10:02,803 --> 00:10:05,673
(thunder rumbling)

245
00:10:08,208 --> 00:10:10,110
- There's something very
strange going on in that light.

246
00:10:10,110 --> 00:10:11,412
Look, over there.

247
00:10:11,412 --> 00:10:12,245
- Didn't you hear me?

248
00:10:12,245 --> 00:10:14,648
Go get that damn ladder.

249
00:10:14,648 --> 00:10:15,515
- Okay.

250
00:10:15,515 --> 00:10:16,683
- Move it!

251
00:10:16,683 --> 00:10:17,618
- Heil Hitler.

252
00:10:17,618 --> 00:10:18,652
- [Joel] I'm going, I'm going.

253
00:10:18,652 --> 00:10:20,087
Jeepers.

254
00:10:20,087 --> 00:10:21,855
- [Tom] First up
on Hearts of Space,

255
00:10:21,855 --> 00:10:24,725
John Tesh with
"Whispering Firestorm."

256
00:10:24,725 --> 00:10:28,295
Then it's Yanni with
"Snoremaster of Trafalgamar."

257
00:10:28,295 --> 00:10:30,832
Then comes bay area
musician Del Mondo,

258
00:10:30,832 --> 00:10:33,433
with his Sominex
suite in D-flat.

259
00:10:33,433 --> 00:10:37,505
Then a synthesized
interplanetary
salute to Perry Como.

260
00:10:37,505 --> 00:10:39,340
At the end of the hour,
we'll have information

261
00:10:39,340 --> 00:10:42,308
about the types of sedatives
used by tonight's artists

262
00:10:42,308 --> 00:10:45,112
on Music from the
Hearts of Space.

263
00:10:49,017 --> 00:10:49,983
(cat meowing)

264
00:10:49,983 --> 00:10:51,985
- [Joel] Football practice.

265
00:10:51,985 --> 00:10:53,553
- [Tom] Puma?

266
00:10:53,553 --> 00:10:54,355
Puma.

267
00:10:58,225 --> 00:10:59,227
- [Crow] Spielberg?

268
00:10:59,227 --> 00:11:01,628
