physical fitness award.

282
00:11:39,767 --> 00:11:41,168
It's a done deal.

283
00:11:42,002 --> 00:11:43,537
(Crow grunts)

284
00:11:43,537 --> 00:11:44,705
(Tom grunts)

285
00:11:44,705 --> 00:11:46,240
- [Crow] Come on, you wuss.

286
00:11:46,240 --> 00:11:47,708
- [Joel] Come on,
you gotta want it.

287
00:11:47,708 --> 00:11:51,478
- [Crow] Hey, Dad hid
the eggs good this year.

288
00:11:57,852 --> 00:11:58,685
- [Tom] Whoa.

289
00:11:58,685 --> 00:12:00,553
- [Joel] That darn cat.

290
00:12:07,928 --> 00:12:08,728
Huh?

291
00:12:10,197 --> 00:12:11,098
- [Tom] Ooh!

292
00:12:11,098 --> 00:12:12,600
- [Crow] Next time on MacGyver.

293
00:12:12,600 --> 00:12:13,600
- [Joel] I do believe in spooks.

294
00:12:13,600 --> 00:12:14,868
I do believe in spooks.

295
00:12:14,868 --> 00:12:16,803
I do, I do, I do, I do,
I do believe in spooks.

296
00:12:16,803 --> 00:12:17,605
I do, I do.

297
00:12:17,605 --> 00:12:18,438
Good night.

298
00:12:18,438 --> 00:12:20,373
- [Tom] Huzzah!

299
00:12:20,373 --> 00:12:21,442
- [Man] Ha!

300
00:12:21,442 --> 00:12:23,510
Did you see that?

301
00:12:23,510 --> 00:12:24,412
- [Tom] Speak Middle English.

302
00:12:24,412 --> 00:12:25,245
- Did you see it?

303
00:12:25,245 --> 00:12:26,513
What?

304
00:12:26,513 --> 00:12:28,048
What the hell are
you talking about?

305
00:12:28,048 --> 00:12:28,982
Looked like like a huge ball
of fire crashed over there.

306
00:12:28,982 --> 00:12:29,917
- Probably a bolt of lightning.

307
00:12:29,917 --> 00:12:31,152
- It was no bolt of lightning.

308
00:12:31,152 --> 00:12:34,788
I tell you something
crashed back there.

309
00:12:34,788 --> 00:12:35,823
- What's going on?

310
00:12:35,823 --> 00:12:36,757
I just saw something.
- Nothing.

311
00:12:36,757 --> 00:12:38,192
- [Crow] Here, hold my purse.

312
00:12:38,192 --> 00:12:40,560
- I swear to you, I saw
something crash back there.

313
00:12:40,560 --> 00:12:41,928
I don't know, maybe a meteorite.

314
00:12:41,928 --> 00:12:42,763
- Forget it, Sam.

315
00:12:42,763 --> 00:12:43,697
Just go and get--

316
00:12:43,697 --> 00:12:44,498
- [Tom] Push him over now.

317
00:12:44,498 --> 00:12:45,298
- The ladder, will you?

318
00:12:45,298 --> 00:12:46,133
Go on.

319
00:12:46,133 --> 00:12:47,067
- [Tom] I love that one.

320
00:12:47,067 --> 00:12:49,203
- And don't take all night.

321
00:12:51,838 --> 00:12:54,375
- Wish we brought Bill along
instead of that crazy moron.

322
00:12:54,375 --> 00:12:55,208
- Bill?

323
00:12:55,208 --> 00:12:56,177
He's changed sides.

324
00:12:56,177 --> 00:12:57,478
Works for the rangers now.

325
00:12:57,478 --> 00:12:58,778
- [Joel] Bill jumped the fence?

326
00:12:58,778 --> 00:12:59,780
- Bill on the side of the law?

327
00:12:59,780 --> 00:13:00,747
That's incredible.

328
00:13:00,747 --> 00:13:01,782
- [Tom] Swings both ways now.

329
00:13:01,782 --> 00:13:04,252
- Let's try that
nest over there.

330
00:13:07,822 --> 00:13:09,857
- [Joel] Hey, looks
like Yoda's home.

331
00:13:09,857 --> 00:13:10,690
Luke?

332
00:13:10,690 --> 00:13:12,325
Use the Force, Luke.

333
00:13:17,565 --> 00:13:18,732
- [Crow] Hmm.

334
00:13:18,732 --> 00:13:19,633
Nah.

335
00:13:19,633 --> 00:13:20,667
Nah.

336
00:13:20,667 --> 00:13:21,968
(Crow snorting)

337
00:13:21,968 --> 00:13:24,672
Ah, ah, it's clearing now.

338
00:13:24,672 --> 00:13:27,642
- [Joel] With a name like
Smuckers raspberry preserves,

339
00:13:27,642 --> 00:13:29,210
you know it's good.

340
00:13:30,410 --> 00:13:32,813
This inflamed
tissue, the burning,

341
00:13:32,813 --> 00:13:35,315
we'd better put some peroxide.

342
00:13:35,315 --> 00:13:37,952
Smuckers brand peroxide.

343
00:13:37,952 --> 00:13:40,087
- [Crow] I'll get a hanky.

344
00:13:45,525 --> 00:13:47,193
- [Tom] Welcome to Laserium.

345
00:13:47,193 --> 00:13:49,797
Tonight, music by Rick Wakeman.

346
00:13:52,667 --> 00:13:55,135
(Tom humming)

347
00:13:58,505 --> 00:13:59,340
- [Crow] A ladder.

348
00:13:59,340 --> 00:14:00,740
That's a rope.

349
00:14:00,740 --> 00:14:01,542
Idiot.

350
00:14:06,413 --> 00:14:07,280
(Tom humming)

351
00:14:07,280 --> 00:14:08,115
- [Tom] Oh, forget this.

352
00:14:08,115 --> 00:14:10,050
I'm gettin' outta here!

353
00:14:16,290 --> 00:14:17,925
- [Joel] I'm no longer
your whipping boy.

354
00:14:17,925 --> 00:14:21,562
I ain't gonna work on
Maggie's farm no more.

355
00:14:26,033 --> 00:14:27,467
(Joel laughing)

356
00:14:27,467 --> 00:14:30,337
- [Joel] If you can't find
'em, grind 'em, right?

357
00:14:30,337 --> 00:14:32,072
Grind a pound for me, man.

358
00:14:32,072 --> 00:14:34,140
- [Tom] This Outward Bound
is really broadening him.

359
00:14:34,140 --> 00:14:35,075
(man gasps)

360
00:14:35,075 --> 00:14:36,343
- Well worth the trouble.

361
00:14:36,343 --> 00:14:38,812
- Hey, let me have a look.

362
00:14:38,812 --> 00:14:40,680
- [Joel] Good idea.

363
00:14:40,680 --> 00:14:41,948
Hmm.

364
00:14:41,948 --> 00:14:42,883
- [Tom] What have we here?

365
00:14:42,883 --> 00:14:45,118
- [Joel] These are kola nuts.

366
00:14:45,118 --> 00:14:46,353
These are un-kola nuts.

367
00:14:46,353 --> 00:14:47,453
- These will pay the
rent for a while.

368
00:14:47,453 --> 00:14:48,388
Where's Sam?

369
00:14:48,388 --> 00:14:49,188
- [Crow] He's paying the rent.

370
00:14:49,188 --> 00:14:50,857
- Hell, I don't know.

371
00:14:50,857 --> 00:14:52,693
Should've been back
by now, though.

372
00:14:52,693 --> 00:14:54,495
Hey, what if the son
of a has run out on us?

373
00:14:54,495 --> 00:14:55,428
- And taken the truck, too.

374
00:14:55,428 --> 00:14:57,932
- [Crow] Don't touch him there.

375
00:14:58,865 --> 00:14:59,700
- Come on.

376
00:15:01,168 --> 00:15:03,737
(upbeat music)

377
00:15:10,843 --> 00:15:13,347
(eerie music)

378
00:15:14,982 --> 00:15:18,052
- [Crow] Now Mr. Science is
gonna show us the white cells.

379
00:15:18,052 --> 00:15:19,887
- [Tom] Put that down.

380
00:15:20,887 --> 00:15:22,088
D'oh.

381
00:15:22,088 --> 00:15:23,523
- [Crow] Oh, clean
up on aisle seven.

382
00:15:23,523 --> 00:15:25,558
- [Joel] It's a
Gold'n Plump chicken!

383
00:15:25,558 --> 00:15:27,060
- [Crow] Ugh.

384
00:15:27,060 --> 00:15:28,295
- [Joel] Ugh.

385
00:15:28,295 --> 00:15:29,195
- [Tom] Ooh, he
should've checked

386
00:15:29,195 --> 00:15:30,097
the freshness date on those.

387
00:15:30,097 --> 00:15:31,665
- [Crow] Over easy.

388
00:15:33,633 --> 00:15:36,370
Oh, what is he, an L.A. cop?

389
00:15:36,370 --> 00:15:38,905
- [Tom] Man exploring
his territory here.

390
00:15:38,905 --> 00:15:40,073
- [Crow] Ouch.

391
00:15:42,308 --> 00:15:46,313
- [Joel] I guess we know which
came first now, don't we?

392
00:15:46,313 --> 00:15:47,513
(all groaning)

393
00:15:47,513 --> 00:15:49,417
(creature growls)

394
00:15:49,417 --> 00:15:50,850
- [Crow] Wanna make a movie,
you gotta break some eggs.

395
00:15:50,850 --> 00:15:52,853
- [Tom] Bawk, bawk, bawk.

396
00:15:52,853 --> 00:15:54,522
Cluck, cluck, cluck.

397
00:15:56,223 --> 00:15:58,258
- [Joel] Oh my goodness,
it's the Easter Bunny,

398
00:15:58,258 --> 00:15:59,993
and is he ever mad.

399
00:15:59,993 --> 00:16:02,028
- [Crow] Hey, this guy
looks like Norm Abrams

400
00:16:02,028 --> 00:16:03,397
getting killed.

401
00:16:03,397 --> 00:16:04,432
- [Tom] Hmm.

402
00:16:04,432 --> 00:16:05,365
- [Crow] Hear that?

403
00:16:05,365 --> 00:16:06,600
- [Crow] Sounds like Norm Abrams

404
00:16:06,600 --> 00:16:08,402
getting killed by
a giant chicken.

405
00:16:08,402 --> 00:16:10,003
- [Tom] I gotta
walk off those eggs.

406
00:16:10,003 --> 00:16:13,673
Whew, my cholesterol
count's way up.

407
00:16:13,673 --> 00:16:16,010
- [Crow] Morning comes
to cheap white trash.

408
00:16:16,010 --> 00:16:16,843
- Was this it?

409
00:16:16,843 --> 00:16:17,678
- Yeah.

410
00:16:18,545 --> 00:16:19,380
- [Crow] Yeah.

411
00:16:19,380 --> 00:16:20,213
- [Matt] I knew it.

412
00:16:20,213 --> 00:16:22,148
Son of a ran out on us.

413
00:16:22,148 --> 00:16:23,483
- [Man] Ah, looks like we
spend the night out here.

414
00:16:23,483 --> 00:16:25,085
- [Joel] You feel
comfortable sharing

415
00:16:25,085 --> 00:16:26,653
a sleeping bag with me?

416
00:16:26,653 --> 00:16:28,088
- [Tom] Ooh.

417
00:16:28,088 --> 00:16:28,788
- [Matt] All the camping
equipment was in the pickup.

418
00:16:28,788 --> 00:16:29,923
- [Man] So what?

419
00:16:29,923 --> 00:16:30,690
Won't be the first
time you've dropped it.

420
00:16:30,690 --> 00:16:31,625
Come on.

421
00:16:31,625 --> 00:16:32,693
- [Tom] D'oh.

422
00:16:34,093 --> 00:16:37,530
Hey, it's White Fang, and
he's stealing those bifocals.

423
00:16:37,530 --> 00:16:40,133
- [Joel] They came to
Earth to steal bifocals.

424
00:16:40,133 --> 00:16:44,405
- [Tom] Well, it's not his
prescription, I don't think.

425
00:16:44,405 --> 00:16:45,638
- [Crow] I've gone blind.

426
00:16:45,638 --> 00:16:46,873
I'm looking at the
back of my retinas.

427
00:16:46,873 --> 00:16:47,742
- [Joel] No, it's
just the movie.

428
00:16:47,742 --> 00:16:48,675
- [Crow] I'm blind.

429
00:16:48,675 --> 00:16:51,645
- [Tom] The movie went blind.

430
00:16:51,645 --> 00:16:52,478
- [Crow] Oh.

431
00:16:52,478 --> 00:16:54,313
Wish I had gone blind.

432
00:16:55,748 --> 00:16:58,852
- [Tomorrow] Luke, finish
your training, you will.

433
00:16:58,852 --> 00:17:01,788
(thunder rumbling)

434
00:17:02,957 --> 00:17:06,627
- [Joel] Bambi, humans
are basically good.

435
00:17:06,627 --> 00:17:08,195
- [Tom] Check that.

436
00:17:09,362 --> 00:17:10,297
- [Crow] You know,
Mom, you never hear

437
00:17:10,297 --> 00:17:13,067
the one with your name on it.

438
00:17:13,067 --> 00:17:13,967
- See that?

439
00:17:15,135 --> 00:17:16,937
Game around here isn't
usually at all nervous.

440
00:17:16,937 --> 00:17:19,338
- [Joel] My bloodlust
cannot be sated.

441
00:17:19,338 --> 00:17:21,007
The light trembling
of a fawn as it lay

442
00:17:21,007 --> 00:17:23,877
dying in my arms, you know.

443
00:17:23,877 --> 00:17:26,045
- [Matt] Christ, you're
beginning to sound like Sam.

444
00:17:26,045 --> 00:17:27,313
- [Tom] Son of Sam.

445
00:17:27,313 --> 00:17:29,248
- Why or what, but I
got a funny feeling,

446
00:17:29,248 --> 00:17:30,683
and I don't like it.

447
00:17:30,683 --> 00:17:35,055
- [Joel] I've gotta kill
something is what I gotta do.

448
00:17:35,788 --> 00:17:37,825
- [Crow] Gino Vannelli?

449
00:17:37,825 --> 00:17:38,792
- [Joel] Yee.

450
00:17:38,792 --> 00:17:41,395
- [Tom] Needs a shave.

451
00:17:41,395 --> 00:17:42,228
- [Joel] Ugh.

452
00:17:42,228 --> 00:17:43,063
- [Tom] Ooh.

453
00:17:43,063 --> 00:17:43,897
Right in the eye.

454
00:17:43,897 --> 00:17:44,732
- [All] Ooh.

455
00:17:44,732 --> 00:17:45,932
- [Tom] Whoa!

456
00:17:45,932 --> 00:17:47,167
Woo.

457
00:17:47,167 --> 00:17:48,602
- [Joel] The helpless
cough of a squirrel

458
00:17:48,602 --> 00:17:52,005
with a crushed face, that's
what life's all about.

459
00:17:54,340 --> 00:17:55,808
- [Matt] What's the big hurry?

460
00:17:55,808 --> 00:17:57,443
- [Man] The big hurry's I
wanna get the hell outta here.

461
00:17:57,443 --> 00:17:58,645
- [Tom] I'm doing
a one-man show.

462
00:17:58,645 --> 00:18:02,048
Leslie Nielsen, Leslie
Nielsen, Leslie Nielsen.

463
00:18:02,048 --> 00:18:03,917
- I tell you, there's
something weird going on.

464
00:18:03,917 --> 00:18:07,253
You stick around if
you like, I'm movin'.

465
00:18:07,253 --> 00:18:08,922
- [Tom] Movin' on.

466
00:18:08,922 --> 00:18:11,658
- [Crow] Hey, you may
wanna wax that bikini hair.

467
00:18:11,658 --> 00:18:12,625
- [Tom] Oof!

468
00:18:13,793 --> 00:18:14,995
Oh, you know, even
the movie "The Fog"

469
00:18:14,995 --> 00:18:16,697
didn't have this much fog.

470
00:18:16,697 --> 00:18:18,032
- [Joel] Uh-huh.

471
00:18:19,800 --> 00:18:22,068
You know, the entry wound
of a shot is a kill.

472
00:18:22,068 --> 00:18:23,770
- Okay.
- Please.

473
00:18:23,770 --> 00:18:25,938
- [Matt] At least we'd
have four walls and a roof.

474
00:18:25,938 --> 00:18:27,440
- [Man] And a jail
cell tomorrow.

475
00:18:27,440 --> 00:18:28,642
- [Matt] Oh yeah,
guess you're right.

476
00:18:28,642 --> 00:18:31,145
- [Tom] Eh, forget about that.

477
00:18:32,445 --> 00:18:33,280
Hi, God.

478
00:18:37,283 --> 00:18:40,687
Look, there's Julie
Andrews, and she's on fire!

479
00:18:40,687 --> 00:18:41,855
- [Crow] Good.

480
00:18:44,792 --> 00:18:46,227
- [Tom] Sorry, Jules.

481
00:18:46,227 --> 00:18:47,560
- [Crow] You know, this scene
didn't originally appear

482
00:18:47,560 --> 00:18:49,295
in the movie, but
they restored it.

483
00:18:49,295 --> 00:18:50,263
Aren't you glad?

484
00:18:50,263 --> 00:18:52,532
- [Tom] Oh, thank you, AMC.

485
00:18:54,668 --> 00:18:55,502
Huh.

486
00:18:56,570 --> 00:18:57,503
Mm-hmm.

487
00:18:57,503 --> 00:18:58,705
- [Crow] Ah, it's the cameraman!

488
00:18:58,705 --> 00:19:01,542
He's looking through
the wrong lens!

489
00:19:01,542 --> 00:19:04,343
- [Joel] Oh, that comb used
to belong to Keith Richards.

490
00:19:04,343 --> 00:19:05,778
- [Crow] Ugh, ew.

491
00:19:07,915 --> 00:19:10,150
- Look what I got
here, Uncle Bill.

492
00:19:10,150 --> 00:19:11,852
- Huh, centipede.

493
00:19:11,852 --> 00:19:14,053
- It's a lithobius forficatus.

494
00:19:14,053 --> 00:19:16,557
- To me, it's a centipede.

495
00:19:16,557 --> 00:19:19,727
It's always been
called a centipede.

496
00:19:19,727 --> 00:19:21,628
- [Crow] He's a loving
and giving caregiver.

497
00:19:21,628 --> 00:19:22,997
- What have you got there?

498
00:19:22,997 --> 00:19:24,765
- A lithobius forficatus.

499
00:19:24,765 --> 00:19:26,032
- [Man] Centipede.

500
00:19:26,032 --> 00:19:27,367
- Well, chuck the
filthy thing away.

501
00:19:27,367 --> 00:19:28,602
- It's for my insect collection.

502
00:19:28,602 --> 00:19:30,403
- Then, take it up
to your room, okay?

503
00:19:30,403 --> 00:19:32,705
- Can I go out and find
some more specimens?

504
00:19:32,705 --> 00:19:34,575
- Later, you've got to help
your uncle in the cellar.

505
00:19:34,575 --> 00:19:37,843
Now then, finish your breakfast.

506
00:19:37,843 --> 00:19:39,245
- [Tom] Aww.

507
00:19:39,245 --> 00:19:40,513
- [Crow] Oops, wrong bowl.

508
00:19:40,513 --> 00:19:43,583
(all groaning)

509
00:19:43,583 --> 00:19:45,385
