- [Tom] Coffee?

1029
00:35:19,852 --> 00:35:22,355
(Laura huffs)

1030
00:35:24,023 --> 00:35:25,257
- Laura!

1031
00:35:25,257 --> 00:35:26,525
- [Tom] You forgot
your breakfast!

1032
00:35:26,525 --> 00:35:27,760
- [Tracy] I think I
better go after her.

1033
00:35:27,760 --> 00:35:30,830
- No, leave her
alone for a while.

1034
00:35:30,830 --> 00:35:32,398
Let her cool off.

1035
00:35:32,398 --> 00:35:34,100
- [Crow] Or get
eaten by creatures.

1036
00:35:34,100 --> 00:35:36,502
- [Tom] Snap an ankle,
die of exposure.

1037
00:35:36,502 --> 00:35:39,005
- You know, we have
been very hard on her.

1038
00:35:39,005 --> 00:35:42,908
- [Crow] Yeah, but it's a good
chance to thin out the cast.

1039
00:35:42,908 --> 00:35:44,110
(Tom imitating weeping)

1040
00:35:44,110 --> 00:35:46,845
- [Tom] I don't
even like coffee.

1041
00:35:50,617 --> 00:35:51,717
(Tom slurping)

1042
00:35:51,717 --> 00:35:52,985
- [Joel] Only half a cup?

1043
00:35:52,985 --> 00:35:54,353
- [Tom] Mm-hmm.

1044
00:35:54,353 --> 00:35:57,490
- [Tom] Don't you
like the rich taste?

1045
00:35:58,858 --> 00:36:00,325
- [Tom] Mmm.

1046
00:36:00,325 --> 00:36:01,293
- [Crow] Dad?

1047
00:36:01,293 --> 00:36:02,462
- [Tom] Mummy?

1048
00:36:04,030 --> 00:36:04,997
- Ricky?

1049
00:36:04,997 --> 00:36:06,398
- [Crow] Mr. Drysdale?

1050
00:36:06,398 --> 00:36:08,733
- [Joel] Mr. Eddie's father?

1051
00:36:10,268 --> 00:36:12,037
- [Laura] Don't play
games with me, please.

1052
00:36:12,037 --> 00:36:13,338
- [Crow] Mr. Douglas.

1053
00:36:13,338 --> 00:36:14,473
- [Tom] Mr. Haney.

1054
00:36:14,473 --> 00:36:15,307
- [Crow] Lisa?

1055
00:36:15,307 --> 00:36:16,142
- [Tom] Chief?

1056
00:36:16,142 --> 00:36:17,910
- [Crow] McCloud?

1057
00:36:17,910 --> 00:36:20,478
(upbeat music)

1058
00:36:23,883 --> 00:36:26,785
(mysterious music)

1059
00:36:27,853 --> 00:36:28,922
- Please come out.

1060
00:36:28,922 --> 00:36:29,955
- [Tom] Shaking the trees.

1061
00:36:29,955 --> 00:36:32,225
- Ricky, I'm frightened.

1062
00:36:32,225 --> 00:36:33,858
(Laura gasps)

1063
00:36:33,858 --> 00:36:35,360
- Hey, look at the
little birdie I caught.

1064
00:36:35,360 --> 00:36:37,062
- [Tom] It's a girl, you idiot.

1065
00:36:37,062 --> 00:36:38,030
- You know what, Matt?

1066
00:36:38,030 --> 00:36:39,298
You're a real blockhead.

1067
00:36:39,298 --> 00:36:40,833
You're just looking
to land up in jail.

1068
00:36:40,833 --> 00:36:42,502
- [Joel] Come on, I
can use her in my act.

1069
00:36:42,502 --> 00:36:43,335
Huzzah.

1070
00:36:43,335 --> 00:36:44,370
- I ain't doing nothing.

1071
00:36:44,370 --> 00:36:45,437
You better run.

1072
00:36:45,437 --> 00:36:46,272
- It's all forest that way.

1073
00:36:46,272 --> 00:36:47,773
She won't get far.

1074
00:36:49,075 --> 00:36:50,142
- [Tom] D'oh.

1075
00:36:51,677 --> 00:36:53,578
- [Matt] Come on.

1076
00:36:53,578 --> 00:36:55,648
- [Crow] And there,
on the handle, was,

1077
00:36:55,648 --> 00:36:56,615
you're not listening.

1078
00:36:56,615 --> 00:36:58,517
- Great weather for a picnic.

1079
00:36:58,517 --> 00:37:00,653
I read it in my horoscope.

1080
00:37:01,853 --> 00:37:03,322
- [Joel] My horoscope
said you'd be stalked

1081
00:37:03,322 --> 00:37:06,292
by a leather mug maker from
a Renaissance Festival.

1082
00:37:06,292 --> 00:37:08,293
(Laura panting)

1083
00:37:08,293 --> 00:37:10,362
- Jesus, that little
can run a lot faster

1084
00:37:10,362 --> 00:37:11,297
than I thought.

1085
00:37:11,297 --> 00:37:12,097
- Yeah, well, you're a jerk.

1086
00:37:12,097 --> 00:37:13,765
- [Tom] Ooh, touche.

1087
00:37:13,765 --> 00:37:14,667
Very clever.

1088
00:37:14,667 --> 00:37:15,500
(Laura gasps)

1089
00:37:15,500 --> 00:37:16,468
(creature growling)

1090
00:37:16,468 --> 00:37:17,803
(Laura screaming)

1091
00:37:17,803 --> 00:37:20,640
- [Tom] Next week on Mannix.

1092
00:37:20,640 --> 00:37:22,073
- God, what was that?

1093
00:37:22,073 --> 00:37:24,143
- [Crow] Sounded like
Laura leaping to her death.

1094
00:37:24,143 --> 00:37:24,977
- Laura?

1095
00:37:25,845 --> 00:37:27,112
- [Tom] Jerk.

1096
00:37:27,112 --> 00:37:27,947
Jerk.

1097
00:37:29,015 --> 00:37:30,282
Over there, jerk.

1098
00:37:30,282 --> 00:37:31,117
Come on, jerk.

1099
00:37:31,117 --> 00:37:32,117
Such a jerk.

1100
00:37:33,885 --> 00:37:34,720
- Come on.

1101
00:37:35,855 --> 00:37:39,625
- [Joel] Wait, did
we leave the iron on?

1102
00:37:39,625 --> 00:37:40,458
- Laura!

1103
00:37:40,458 --> 00:37:41,827
Where are you, Laura?

1104
00:37:41,827 --> 00:37:43,328
- [Joel] Tell Laura I love her.

1105
00:37:43,328 --> 00:37:44,663
- [Brian] Laura!

1106
00:37:44,663 --> 00:37:45,497
- [Tom] Huh?

1107
00:37:45,497 --> 00:37:46,698
Is your name Laura?

1108
00:37:46,698 --> 00:37:47,633
- [Man] Nothing
but trouble, Matt.

1109
00:37:47,633 --> 00:37:49,302
Let's get outta here fast.

1110
00:37:50,168 --> 00:37:51,337
- [Joel] Bitty-bitty-bitty.

1111
00:37:51,337 --> 00:37:52,838
Wanna dance, Buck?

1112
00:37:55,307 --> 00:37:56,975
- [Tom] Oh, it's Laura Palmer.

1113
00:37:56,975 --> 00:37:57,810
(thunder rumbling)

1114
00:37:57,810 --> 00:37:58,810
Soupy Sales.

1115
00:38:04,783 --> 00:38:05,718
- This way.

1116
00:38:05,718 --> 00:38:07,520
- [Crow] What, do you smell her?

1117
00:38:07,520 --> 00:38:08,487
- [Tom] Yeah, like a bloodhound.

1118
00:38:08,487 --> 00:38:09,655
- [Crow] Yeah.

1119
00:38:10,588 --> 00:38:11,790
- [Rick] There she is.

1120
00:38:11,790 --> 00:38:12,625
- [Tom] Don't move.

1121
00:38:12,625 --> 00:38:13,925
We'll come down.

1122
00:38:15,962 --> 00:38:17,295
- [Brian] Laura!

1123
00:38:19,132 --> 00:38:19,965
Laura!

1124
00:38:21,967 --> 00:38:22,868
She isn't dead, is she?

1125
00:38:22,868 --> 00:38:23,802
- I don't think so.

1126
00:38:23,802 --> 00:38:24,603
But she's sure in bad shape.

1127
00:38:24,603 --> 00:38:26,105
Get her legs.

1128
00:38:26,105 --> 00:38:27,607
- [Crow] Yeah, quick, move
her spine around a lot.

1129
00:38:27,607 --> 00:38:28,840
(imitating bones cracking)

1130
00:38:28,840 --> 00:38:30,608
- [Crow] Dope.

1131
00:38:30,608 --> 00:38:31,977
- [Tracy] Laura!

1132
00:38:31,977 --> 00:38:32,812
Rick!

1133
00:38:32,812 --> 00:38:33,645
- [Tom] Bosley?

1134
00:38:33,645 --> 00:38:34,547
- [Joel] Angels?

1135
00:38:34,547 --> 00:38:35,380
- [Tom] Chief?

1136
00:38:35,380 --> 00:38:36,215
- [Crow] McCloud?

1137
00:38:36,215 --> 00:38:37,850
- Daddy, where are you?

1138
00:38:37,850 --> 00:38:38,683
- [Tom] Daddy?

1139
00:38:38,683 --> 00:38:40,018
- [Joel] Leviathan?

1140
00:38:40,018 --> 00:38:40,853
- [Tom] Laverne?

1141
00:38:40,853 --> 00:38:41,753
- Where are they?

1142
00:38:41,753 --> 00:38:43,988
- There they are over there.

1143
00:38:45,523 --> 00:38:47,192
Oh, my god, what happened?

1144
00:38:47,192 --> 00:38:48,327
I don't know.

1145
00:38:48,327 --> 00:38:51,230
- [Tom] She's claiming
she's Anais Nin.

1146
00:38:52,432 --> 00:38:53,865
- Things could get
kinda tricky now.

1147
00:38:53,865 --> 00:38:56,002
This place is gonna be
swarming with rangers soon.

1148
00:38:56,002 --> 00:38:57,670
We better be on
our way outta here.

1149
00:38:57,670 --> 00:38:59,472
- [Joel] We shouldn't have
stole that pic-a-nic basket.

1150
00:38:59,472 --> 00:39:02,808
- We'll make for the old
hideout in the canyon, Big Bend.

1151
00:39:02,808 --> 00:39:03,742
- [Joel] Huzzah.

1152
00:39:03,742 --> 00:39:04,743
- Christ, that's miles away.

1153
00:39:04,743 --> 00:39:05,577
(thunder rumbling)

1154
00:39:05,577 --> 00:39:06,412
- Come on.

1155
00:39:12,952 --> 00:39:15,453
- [Tom] Quick, let's fold her.

1156
00:39:20,292 --> 00:39:24,963
- [Crow] Well, I'm so glad they
turned her into a vegetable.

1157
00:39:24,963 --> 00:39:26,365
- Give me one of the blankets.

1158
00:39:26,365 --> 00:39:27,198
- [Tom] No, that's okay.

1159
00:39:27,198 --> 00:39:28,033
I'm not cold.

1160
00:39:28,033 --> 00:39:28,867
- [Crow] It's for her.

1161
00:39:28,867 --> 00:39:29,768
- [Tom] Oh.

1162
00:39:32,370 --> 00:39:33,605
TRACY: Here,
this'll warm her up.

1163
00:39:33,605 --> 00:39:34,840
- [Tom] No thanks,
I'm not thirsty.

1164
00:39:34,840 --> 00:39:36,742
- [Crow] It's for her, for her.

1165
00:39:36,742 --> 00:39:38,777
- [Joel] For her.

1166
00:39:38,777 --> 00:39:39,845
- [Tom] She obviously
doesn't need it.

1167
00:39:39,845 --> 00:39:41,413
- [Brian] She's out cold.

1168
00:39:41,413 --> 00:39:42,648
- [Crow] Yeah.

1169
00:39:42,648 --> 00:39:43,415
- We've got to get
her to a hospital.

1170
00:39:43,415 --> 00:39:44,650
- [Joel] Or a bar.

1171
00:39:44,650 --> 00:39:46,085
- Hold on, Rick, it's
more than 50 miles.

1172
00:39:46,085 --> 00:39:49,155
In this weather, on these roads,
you wouldn't get very far.

1173
00:39:49,155 --> 00:39:50,222
- We have to do
something, Brian.

1174
00:39:50,222 --> 00:39:52,257
We can't just leave her.

1175
00:39:52,257 --> 00:39:53,192
- It's my fault.

1176
00:39:53,192 --> 00:39:54,360
I forced her to run away.

1177
00:39:54,360 --> 00:39:55,327
- Oh, Sharon, it
wasn't you, it was me.

1178
00:39:55,327 --> 00:39:56,162
She'll be all right, you'll see.

1179
00:39:56,162 --> 00:39:58,063
- [Joel] It's her fault.

1180
00:39:58,063 --> 00:39:59,232
- What can we do, Brian?

1181
00:39:59,232 --> 00:40:00,732
- [Crow] Jam a sandwich
down her throat.

1182
00:40:00,732 --> 00:40:03,702
- The refuge at Black Butte,
where there's a telephone,

1183
00:40:03,702 --> 00:40:04,837
and they can help us.

1184
00:40:04,837 --> 00:40:05,737
- Then, let's get out things.

1185
00:40:05,737 --> 00:40:06,572
Come on.

1186
00:40:09,375 --> 00:40:11,977
- [Tom] Meanwhile,
in another movie.

1187
00:40:11,977 --> 00:40:14,012
Ah, patience, gentle viewer.

1188
00:40:14,012 --> 00:40:16,182
This'll all make sense
in the end. (cuckles)

1189
00:40:16,182 --> 00:40:17,015
Not.

1190
00:40:18,383 --> 00:40:22,455
- [Crow] I wonder when Flo
and Alice are gonna get here.

1191
00:40:22,455 --> 00:40:24,223
- [Tom] Mel, at home.

1192
00:40:28,160 --> 00:40:29,093
Let me out!

1193
00:40:31,597 --> 00:40:33,065
I said let me out!

1194
00:40:34,667 --> 00:40:36,135
I said let me out!

1195
00:40:38,103 --> 00:40:39,070
Ow, ow.

1196
00:40:39,070 --> 00:40:40,305
- [Crow] Shave and a haircut?

1197
00:40:40,305 --> 00:40:41,707
- [Tom] Two bits.

1198
00:40:46,112 --> 00:40:47,412
- [Woman] Tommy.

1199
00:40:48,613 --> 00:40:51,950
- [Crow] Just tending
the incubus, mother.

1200
00:40:55,888 --> 00:40:57,422
- Why haven't you
gone to bed yet?

1201
00:40:57,422 --> 00:40:59,192
- I did, Mom, but
kitty was meowing

1202
00:40:59,192 --> 00:41:00,927
and I thought maybe
he was hungry.

1203
00:41:00,927 --> 00:41:03,895
- Oh, he's already eaten
at least three times today.

1204
00:41:03,895 --> 00:41:05,563
- Then he certainly
shouldn't have any more.

1205
00:41:05,563 --> 00:41:07,298
- Okay, come on, into bed.

1206
00:41:07,298 --> 00:41:10,402
One of these days we're going
to have trouble with you two.

1207
00:41:10,402 --> 00:41:12,137
In you get.

1208
00:41:12,137 --> 00:41:13,772
- [Tom] And remember,
no wire hangers!

1209
00:41:13,772 --> 00:41:14,940
- Settle down.

1210
00:41:17,142 --> 00:41:18,310
Now, go to sleep, all right?

1211
00:41:18,310 --> 00:41:19,178
- Yes, Mom.

1212
00:41:21,247 --> 00:41:22,347
- [Tom] Good night, mother.

1213
00:41:22,347 --> 00:41:24,217
- [Joel] Good night, John-boy.

1214
00:41:24,217 --> 00:41:25,150
- [Tom] Good night, Hardcastle.

1215
00:41:25,150 --> 00:41:26,285
- [Joel] Good night, McCormick.

1216
00:41:26,285 --> 00:41:27,218
- [Tom] Good night, Chief.

1217
00:41:27,218 --> 00:41:28,220
- [Crow] Good night, McCloud.

1218
00:41:28,220 --> 00:41:30,890
(Tom chuckling)

1219
00:41:35,760 --> 00:41:37,730
- You all just wait and see.

1220
00:41:37,730 --> 00:41:39,465
You're gonna have
a new friend soon.

1221
00:41:39,465 --> 00:41:40,698
(Crow chuckles)

1222
00:41:40,698 --> 00:41:42,735
- [Crow] That's really
great, little kid.

1223
00:41:42,735 --> 00:41:44,135
- [Tom] Sad.

1224
00:41:44,135 --> 00:41:46,305
- [Joel] Spends a
lot of time alone.

1225
00:41:46,305 --> 00:41:47,105
Ugh.

1226
00:41:48,307 --> 00:41:50,208
Oh, he's trying
to hatch the egg.

1227
00:41:50,208 --> 00:41:51,777
What is he, Horton?

1228
00:41:51,777 --> 00:41:55,180
(Tom chuckling)

1229
00:41:55,180 --> 00:41:56,282
(Tom snores)

1230
00:41:56,282 --> 00:41:58,283
- [Tom] Okay, so
is this Movie A?

1231
00:41:58,283 --> 00:42:00,185
- [Joel] Beats me.

1232
00:42:00,185 --> 00:42:01,220
- [Tom] Well, let's see.

1233
00:42:01,220 --> 00:42:02,487
The hunters are in Movie A.

1234
00:42:02,487 --> 00:42:04,557
The kid was in Movie B.

1235
00:42:04,557 --> 00:42:06,292
- [Crow] Ah, this is
the Cowsills part.

1236
00:42:06,292 --> 00:42:08,227
This is Movie C, C.

1237
00:42:08,227 --> 00:42:09,595
- [Joel] I shouldn't
have had so much coffee.

1238
00:42:09,595 --> 00:42:11,163
I'll be right back.

1239
00:42:12,565 --> 00:42:13,665
- [Tom] Ooh, enter
the fog machine.

1240
00:42:13,665 --> 00:42:16,068
(mysterious music)

1241
00:42:16,068 --> 00:42:17,068
- [Joel] Come on, honey.

1242
00:42:17,068 --> 00:42:19,238
You're gonna love it here.

1243
00:42:20,272 --> 00:42:21,073
- Hello?

1244
00:42:23,442 --> 00:42:24,510
Anybody home?

1245
00:42:26,678 --> 00:42:28,313
- What do you want at
this time of night?

1246
00:42:28,313 --> 00:42:29,515
- We need help.

1247
00:42:29,515 --> 00:42:31,983
- Well, go and find
it somewhere else.

1248
00:42:31,983 --> 00:42:34,118
- Wait a minute, please!

1249
00:42:34,118 --> 00:42:35,453
Please, we need help!

1250
00:42:35,453 --> 00:42:37,455
- What's going on, Bill?

1251
00:42:37,455 --> 00:42:38,457
- Just a troublemaker.

1252
00:42:38,457 --> 00:42:39,392
- [Crow] Nah, Jehovah Witnesses.

1253
00:42:39,392 --> 00:42:40,292
- [Rick] Please, we need help.

1254
00:42:40,292 --> 00:42:41,627
- Open the door, Bill.

1255
00:42:41,627 --> 00:42:42,460
Go on.

1256
00:42:43,462 --> 00:42:45,397
- [Joel] Open the door.

1257
00:42:46,598 --> 00:42:48,433
- Please, ma'am, can
we use your phone?

1258
00:42:48,433 --> 00:42:49,402
There's been an accident.

1259
00:42:49,402 --> 00:42:50,335
- [Joel] She soiled herself.

1260
00:42:50,335 --> 00:42:51,370
- What kind of trouble?

1261
00:42:51,370 --> 00:42:52,370
- [Tom] Oh, please.

1262
00:42:52,370 --> 00:42:54,707
- She fell.
- Bring her in.

1263
00:42:54,707 --> 00:42:56,042
- [Tom] Accident.

1264
00:42:57,743 --> 00:42:58,743
- Follow me.

1265
00:43:07,552 --> 00:43:08,687
- This phone isn't working.

1266
00:43:08,687 --> 00:43:09,922
- [Crow] Give me that.

1267
00:43:09,922 --> 00:43:12,658
I'll show you how
to use a prop phone.

1268
00:43:12,658 --> 00:43:13,492
- All right?

1269
00:43:13,492 --> 00:43:14,993
- Yeah, fine.

1270
00:43:14,993 --> 00:43:17,162
- [Crow] Yeah, just a few more
rooms, and you'll be there.

1271
00:43:17,162 --> 00:43:18,063
Keep going.

1272
00:43:22,267 --> 00:43:23,768
- [Tom] Ooh, nice.

1273
00:43:26,705 --> 00:43:28,240
- The line's dead.

1274
00:43:28,240 --> 00:43:29,742
- There's been a rock fall.

1275
00:43:29,742 --> 00:43:31,243
The road's blocked.

1276
00:43:31,243 --> 00:43:33,412
The phone lines are
probably down, too.

1277
00:43:33,412 --> 00:43:35,113
- [Joel] There's no
way out of this film.

1278
00:43:35,113 --> 00:43:38,217
- God only knows how
you got this far.

1279
00:43:41,320 --> 00:43:43,222
- Did you get through
to the hospital?

1280
00:43:43,222 --> 00:43:44,423
- [Crow] No, it's a prop phone.

1281
00:43:44,423 --> 00:43:45,757
- No way.

1282
00:43:45,757 --> 00:43:47,125
The phone's screwed up.

1283
00:43:47,125 --> 00:43:48,593
- That's all we need.

1284
00:43:48,727 --> 00:43:51,063
- [Joel] Oh man, if it's
not one thing, it's another.

1285
00:43:52,898 --> 00:43:54,600
- [Brian] Surely must be
some way of getting help.

1286
00:43:54,600 --> 00:43:55,600
- [Tom] Hey, life stinks, man.

1287
00:43:55,600 --> 00:43:56,468
Deal with it.

1288
00:43:56,468 --> 00:43:57,235
- Not now there ain't.

1289
00:43:57,235 --> 00:43:58,303
- You sure?

1290
00:43:58,303 --> 00:43:59,972
- Of course I am.

1291
00:43:59,972 --> 00:44:02,473
- Come on, I'll make
you some coffee.

1292
00:44:02,473 --> 00:44:04,042
Don't worry.

1293
00:44:04,042 --> 00:44:05,677
She'll be all right.

1294
00:44:07,012 --> 00:44:08,847
- [Tom] Mm-hmm.

1295
00:44:08,847 --> 00:44:09,915
- [Woman] With a good
night's rest, she'll be

1296
00:44:09,915 --> 00:44:11,750
as right as rain in the morning.

1297
00:44:11,750 --> 00:44:14,085
- [Joel] Yeah, that's what
cures a crushed spine.

1298
00:44:14,085 --> 00:44:15,353
- [Tom] Uh-huh.

1299
00:44:23,662 --> 00:44:24,730
- What's going on?

1300
00:44:24,730 --> 00:44:25,530
- Nothing.

1301
00:44:25,530 --> 00:44:26,732
The phone's not working.

1302
00:44:26,732 --> 00:44:28,533
The road back to
town is blocked.

1303
00:44:28,533 --> 00:44:30,035
Looks like there's
no way out of here.

1304
00:44:30,035 --> 00:44:31,103
- But Laura needs help.

1305
00:44:31,103 --> 00:44:32,203
There must be some way.

1306
00:44:32,203 --> 00:44:33,138
- Doesn't look like it.

1307
00:44:33,138 --> 00:44:34,407
Not in this bloody wilderness.

1308
00:44:34,407 --> 00:44:37,042
You and your out
of the way places.

1309
00:44:37,042 --> 00:44:37,977
- [Tom] D'oh.

1310
00:44:37,977 --> 00:44:39,378
- [Sharon] Come on now, Rick--

1311
00:44:39,378 --> 00:44:41,113
- [Joel] Wow, a rock
group staying at my house?

1312
00:44:41,113 --> 00:44:41,947
Too much.

1313
00:44:43,048 --> 00:44:45,850
- [Rick] I know,
I'm not blaming you.

1314
00:44:45,850 --> 00:44:47,552
- It'll all be all right.

1315
00:44:47,552 --> 00:44:48,887
I know where we can get help.

1316
00:44:48,887 --> 00:44:49,955
- Please, Mrs...

1317
00:44:49,955 --> 00:44:50,788
- Stevens.

1318
00:44:50,788 --> 00:44:51,623
- Thank you.

1319
00:44:51,623 --> 00:44:52,423
- Molly Stevens.

1320
00:44:52,423 --> 00:44:53,458
- Tell us, Mrs. Stevens.

1321
00:44:53,458 --> 00:44:54,727
- [Joel] Molly Stevens.

1322
00:44:54,727 --> 00:44:55,527
- Just a few miles
from here there's

1323
00:44:55,527 --> 00:44:56,562
a forest ranger's cabin.

1324
00:44:56,562 --> 00:44:57,528
They've got a radio.

1325
00:44:57,528 --> 00:44:58,830
- Then what are we waiting for?

1326
00:44:58,830 --> 00:44:59,998
- Not now.

1327
00:44:59,998 --> 00:45:01,733
You'll have to
wait for daylight.

1328
00:45:01,733 --> 00:45:03,502
At night you wouldn't make it.

1329
00:45:03,502 --> 00:45:04,903
Anyway, since it's springtime,

1330
00:45:04,903 --> 00:45:07,205
the rangers will be out
searching for poachers.

1331
00:45:07,205 --> 00:45:08,373
I'm right, Bill, aren't I?

1332
00:45:08,373 --> 00:45:09,608
- [Crow] Oh, yeah,
I'll give you that one.

1333
00:45:09,608 --> 00:45:11,210
- Bill knows where
the patrols get to.

1334
00:45:11,210 --> 00:45:12,610
He'll take you there tomorrow.

1335
00:45:12,610 --> 00:45:14,012
Now you must get some rest.

1336
00:45:14,012 --> 00:45:16,282
It's no good worrying.

1337
00:45:16,282 --> 00:45:18,117
We've got plenty of space here.

1338
00:45:18,117 --> 00:45:19,183
So as soon as you
finish your coffee,

1339
00:45:19,183 --> 00:45:20,818
I'll show you to your room.

1340
00:45:20,818 --> 00:45:23,588
- [Brian] You're
being very kind.

1341
00:45:28,793 --> 00:45:29,728
- [Tom] Egg?

1342
00:45:29,728 --> 00:45:30,662
Say, egg.

1343
00:45:30,662 --> 00:45:31,563
There's a lot of people here.

1344
00:45:31,563 --> 00:45:32,397
(boy gasps)

1345
00:45:32,397 --> 00:45:33,198
Huh?

1346
00:45:34,900 --> 00:45:36,302
Ooh, we gotta go.

1347
00:45:38,570 --> 00:45:40,005
(all groaning)

1348
00:45:40,005 --> 00:45:42,440
- [Joel] Creamy living
chocolate center.

1349
00:45:42,440 --> 00:45:43,442
- [Tom] Ugh!

1350
00:45:50,682 --> 00:45:53,285
(upbeat music)

1351
00:45:57,655 --> 00:45:58,823
- Oh, hiya, Crow.

1352
00:45:58,823 --> 00:45:59,658
- Oh, hi.

1353
00:45:59,658 --> 00:46:01,160
- Whatcha doin'?

1354
00:46:01,160 --> 00:46:02,795
- Oh, we were just inspired
by the cool new-age music

1355
00:46:02,795 --> 00:46:05,963
of this movie, so we decided
to use the wall of keyboards

1356
00:46:05,963 --> 00:46:08,267
and make out own great
new new-age music.

1357
00:46:08,267 --> 00:46:09,100
You wanna help?

1358
00:46:09,100 --> 00:46:09,935
- Sure.

1359
00:46:09,935 --> 00:46:11,470
What can I do?

1360
00:46:11,470 --> 00:46:12,637
- Well, I could teach you
how to play the keyboards.

1361
00:46:12,637 --> 00:46:13,538
- Will it take long?

1362
00:46:13,538 --> 00:46:14,540
- No, of course not.

1363
00:46:14,540 --> 00:46:15,773
Come on over here.

1364
00:46:15,773 --> 00:46:17,275
Here, check this out.

1365
00:46:17,275 --> 00:46:19,010
Okay, put your hand, come
on, put your hand over here.

1366
00:46:19,010 --> 00:46:19,912
- [Crow] Okay.

1367
00:46:19,912 --> 00:46:21,012
- Put your finger down, see?

1368
00:46:21,012 --> 00:46:21,813
- Like that?
- Yeah.

1369
00:46:21,813 --> 00:46:23,048
- Ah.

1370
00:46:23,048 --> 00:46:24,483
- Yeah, you got
it, you're playing

1371
00:46:24,483 --> 00:46:26,152
a new-age chord now, okay?

1372
00:46:26,152 --> 00:46:26,985
- Hey.

1373
00:46:26,985 --> 00:46:28,253
- Just like Yanni.

1374
00:46:28,253 --> 00:46:30,822
All right, now, put
another finger down.

1375
00:46:30,822 --> 00:46:31,657
- Okay.

1376
00:46:31,657 --> 00:46:32,557
- See?

1377
00:46:32,557 --> 00:46:33,492
Now you're playing a Yanni lick.

1378
00:46:33,492 --> 00:46:35,093
Now, hold it down for an hour.

1379
00:46:35,093 --> 00:46:36,595
- Yeah.

1380
00:46:36,595 --> 00:46:37,897
- Now hold it down till
you get a record contract

1381
00:46:37,897 --> 00:46:39,197
from Windham Hill.

1382
00:46:39,197 --> 00:46:41,700
- Oh, hey, cool.
- See?

1383
00:46:41,700 --> 00:46:42,633
- Servo, check it out.

1384
00:46:42,633 --> 00:46:44,468
It's my new new-age Yanni lick.

1385
00:46:44,468 --> 00:46:46,738
Joel, hold on my new
new-age Yanni lick.

1386
00:46:46,738 --> 00:46:47,940
I gotta put my sandwich down.

1387
00:46:47,940 --> 00:46:49,173
- Okay, got it.

1388
00:46:49,173 --> 00:46:50,675
- This music's kind
of dull, isn't it?

1389
00:46:50,675 --> 00:46:52,077
- Yeah, but it's a good
way to make a lot of money

1390
00:46:52,077 --> 00:46:54,980
without a big
initial investment.

1391
00:46:54,980 --> 00:46:56,147
(Tom clearing throat)

1392
00:46:56,147 --> 00:46:57,415
- Okay.

1393
00:46:57,415 --> 00:47:00,952
And now, "Music From
Some Guys in Space."

1394
00:47:00,952 --> 00:47:03,588
Tonight on "Music From
Some Guys in Space,"

1395
00:47:03,588 --> 00:47:06,925
more fine new new-age
music and sounds

1396
00:47:06,925 --> 00:47:09,762
from super progressive bay
area new-age keyboardist

1397
00:47:09,762 --> 00:47:11,563
Joel Robinson.

1398
00:47:11,563 --> 00:47:14,032
Joel will be accompanied
on the wall of keyboards

1399
00:47:14,032 --> 00:47:17,035
by veteran minimalist
Crow T. Robot.

1400
00:47:18,503 --> 00:47:20,705
We invite you to sit back
and enjoy more repetitive

1401
00:47:20,705 --> 00:47:24,910
new-age music as we
cruise the space ways.

1402
00:47:24,910 --> 00:47:27,880
Come along, fellow
travelers, and enjoy music

1403
00:47:27,880 --> 00:47:29,882
from some guys in space.

1404
00:47:31,015 --> 00:47:32,283
(alarm blaring)

1405
00:47:32,283 --> 00:47:34,118
- Hey, we got movie
sign, you guys.

1406
00:47:34,118 --> 00:47:37,388
- It's movie sign, next
time on Emergency 911.

1407
00:47:37,388 --> 00:47:39,592
- Tom, you're stuck
in Shatner mode.

1408
00:47:39,592 --> 00:47:41,092
Come on, man, snap out of it.

1409
00:47:41,092 --> 00:47:42,627
Crow, wake up!
- Movie sign!

1410
00:47:42,627 --> 00:47:43,462
- What?

1411
00:47:43,462 --> 00:47:46,030
(all shouting)

1412
00:47:53,305 --> 00:47:56,675
- When I get a hold of that
Sam, I swear I'll kill him.

1413
00:47:56,675 --> 00:47:58,610
Standing us up here like this.

1414
00:47:58,610 --> 00:48:00,245
- Oh, it's not so bad.

1415
00:48:00,245 --> 00:48:02,580
There's a connection
I know who'll give us

1416
00:48:02,580 --> 00:48:03,615
at least, I'd say--

1417
00:48:03,615 --> 00:48:04,850
- [Tom] You awake, Crow?

1418
00:48:04,850 --> 00:48:05,750
- 3000 bucks for this lot.
- Yeah.

1419
00:48:05,750 --> 00:48:07,585
(Crow sighs)

1420
00:48:07,585 --> 00:48:10,155
- And how are we supposed
to get back to town, huh?

1421
00:48:10,155 --> 00:48:10,988
On foot?

1422
00:48:12,223 --> 00:48:15,660
- [Tom] Wait a minute, I'm, yep.

1423
00:48:15,660 --> 00:48:17,662
- It wouldn't be the first time.

1424
00:48:17,662 --> 00:48:19,965
(Tom chuckles)

1425
00:48:19,965 --> 00:48:22,567
- Why don't we take
the kids' camper?

1426
00:48:22,567 --> 00:48:24,002
- Are you crazy?

1427
00:48:24,002 --> 00:48:25,870
- [Joel] Can I think about it?

1428
00:48:25,870 --> 00:48:28,140
- Haven't you screwed
things up enough already?

1429
00:48:28,140 --> 00:48:29,307
Huh?

1430
00:48:29,307 --> 00:48:30,508
- [Crow] Well, he
did write the script.

1431
00:48:30,508 --> 00:48:31,843
- [Joel] Huzzah.

1432
00:48:33,378 --> 00:48:35,847
- What was that noise?

1433
00:48:35,847 --> 00:48:38,750
- Maybe it's the rangers.

1434
00:48:38,750 --> 00:48:40,585
- [Joel] Hey, Boo-Boo.

1435
00:48:43,055 --> 00:48:44,055
- [Tom] Eww.

1436
00:48:46,492 --> 00:48:47,325
Mm-hmm.

1437
00:48:47,325 --> 00:48:49,928
- What on Earth is that?

1438
00:48:49,928 --> 00:48:51,997
Looks like a cross
between a pig and a bear.

1439
00:48:51,997 --> 00:48:52,863
- [Crow] A pear?

1440
00:48:52,863 --> 00:48:54,332
- My god it's ugly.

1441
00:48:54,332 --> 00:48:58,970
- [Joel] Hey, you're no prize
yourself, Dan Folgelberg.

1442
00:48:59,570 --> 00:49:00,872
- Be careful.

1443
00:49:00,872 --> 00:49:01,973
It could be dangerous.

1444
00:49:01,973 --> 00:49:03,442
(gun clicks)

1445
00:49:03,442 --> 00:49:05,743
- Ah, it may be ugly, but
it appears harmless enough.

1446
00:49:05,743 --> 00:49:07,512
- [Joel] Hey, it's
Mr. Snuffleupagus.

1447
00:49:07,512 --> 00:49:08,447
- [Tom] Cute.

1448
00:49:08,447 --> 00:49:09,748
- Sure is a strange bird.

1449
00:49:09,748 --> 00:49:11,950
Think it could be
worth something?

1450
00:49:11,950 --> 00:49:13,118
- Yeah, maybe.

1451
00:49:13,985 --> 00:49:14,820
- [Tom] Maybe.

1452
00:49:14,820 --> 00:49:16,522
- Keep him busy.

1453
00:49:16,522 --> 00:49:17,455
- [Tom] Keep him busy?

1454
00:49:17,455 --> 00:49:19,057
- Hey, enjoying yourself?

1455
00:49:19,057 --> 00:49:20,692
Take a little night stroll?

1456
00:49:20,692 --> 00:49:23,395
Trouble is, the weather's a
little bit rough for that.

1457
00:49:23,395 --> 00:49:24,628
Isn't it?

1458
00:49:24,628 --> 00:49:26,230
- [Crow] Stop the
inane conversation.

1459
00:49:26,230 --> 00:49:27,498
- Go on talking.

1460
00:49:27,498 --> 00:49:30,868
- [Joel] You live
around here much?

1461
00:49:30,868 --> 00:49:33,672
- You must be hungry, huh?

1462
00:49:33,672 --> 00:49:35,007
Have some.

1463
00:49:35,007 --> 00:49:36,842
- [Crow] It's one
of you, only gamier.

1464
00:49:36,842 --> 00:49:37,775
- [Tom] Ew.

1465
00:49:37,775 --> 00:49:38,977
- [Matt] It won't hurt ya.

1466
00:49:38,977 --> 00:49:40,612
- [Joel] So, you
like Chinese food?

1467
00:49:40,612 --> 00:49:42,280
- [Matt] Help yourself.

1468
00:49:42,280 --> 00:49:43,215
- [Joel] Huh?

1469
00:49:43,215 --> 00:49:44,082
- [Tom] Mongolian barbecue?

1470
00:49:44,082 --> 00:49:44,917
- [Joel] Ha.

1471
00:49:44,917 --> 00:49:45,917
- [Tom] Oh.

1472
00:49:45,917 --> 00:49:47,052
- Matt, come on!

1473
00:49:47,052 --> 00:49:47,985
Give me a hand!

1474
00:49:47,985 --> 00:49:49,888
- [Crow] Get the drawn butter.

1475
00:49:49,888 --> 00:49:52,057
- Christ, he's strong.

1476
00:49:52,057 --> 00:49:53,458
I can't hold him.

1477
00:49:55,593 --> 00:49:56,595
- [Tom] Alf, no!

1478
00:49:56,595 --> 00:49:57,628
No, Alf!

1479
00:49:57,628 --> 00:49:58,630
(creature grunts)

1480
00:49:58,630 --> 00:50:00,065
- [Tom] Ooh.

1481
00:50:00,065 --> 00:50:01,733
Big mistake.

1482
00:50:01,733 --> 00:50:03,235
- [Crow] Hey, that
long nose must be handy

1483
00:50:03,235 --> 00:50:04,737
in hard-to-reach areas.

1484
00:50:04,737 --> 00:50:07,372
(Tom chuckling)

1485
00:50:08,940 --> 00:50:10,308
(Tom humming)

1486
00:50:10,308 --> 00:50:11,710
- [Tom] Just pad out the
scene here a little bit.

1487
00:50:11,710 --> 00:50:14,212
(all humming)

1488
00:50:16,715 --> 00:50:18,817
- [Joel] Hey, what gives?

1489
00:50:18,817 --> 00:50:20,718
I'm on the milk carton.

1490
00:50:31,897 --> 00:50:33,632
- You're hungry
again, aren't you?

1491
00:50:33,632 --> 00:50:36,935
There's no need
to worry, Trumpy.

1492
00:50:36,935 --> 00:50:39,170
You like that name,
don't you, Trumpy?

1493
00:50:39,170 --> 00:50:41,573
- [Crow] I prefer Milky Bear.

1494
00:50:42,473 --> 00:50:44,575
- I won't let anyone hurt you.

1495
00:50:44,575 --> 00:50:47,545
- [Joel] I named you
after Donald Trump.

1496
00:50:47,545 --> 00:50:48,347
- Hello.

1497
00:50:50,382 --> 00:50:51,917
Hey, look.

1498
00:50:51,917 --> 00:50:53,152
Look what I got for you.

1499
00:50:53,152 --> 00:50:54,385
- [Tom] Mucus.

1500
00:50:54,385 --> 00:50:55,853
- Oh, boy.

1501
00:50:55,853 --> 00:50:58,523
You sure are greedy, aren't you?

1502
00:50:59,858 --> 00:51:02,693
Wow, if you keep
drinking milk like that,

1503
00:51:02,693 --> 00:51:05,197
you're gonna grow
really big and strong.

1504
00:51:05,197 --> 00:51:07,098
Then we can play together.

1505
00:51:07,098 --> 00:51:08,967
You know what
playing is, Trumpy?

1506
00:51:08,967 --> 00:51:11,503
- [Crow] Yes, it's where
I break you in half.

1507
00:51:11,503 --> 00:51:12,970
- No?

1508
00:51:12,970 --> 00:51:14,172
I'll teach you.

1509
00:51:15,073 --> 00:51:17,075
We're gonna have such fun.

1510
00:51:17,075 --> 00:51:18,042
- [Tom] Foreigner.

1511
00:51:18,042 --> 00:51:19,743
Meanwhile in Movie C.

1512
00:51:20,712 --> 00:51:22,313
- [Crow] I think
this is Movie D.

1513
00:51:22,313 --> 00:51:23,148
- [Tom] Oh.

1514
00:51:23,148 --> 00:51:24,482
- [Crow] D for dumb.

1515
00:51:24,482 --> 00:51:27,385
(Tom chuckling)

1516
00:51:27,385 --> 00:51:28,453
- [Tom] Okay.

1517
00:51:29,653 --> 00:51:31,055
(boy gasps)

1518
00:51:31,055 --> 00:51:31,990
- [Joel] Oh, great.

1519
00:51:31,990 --> 00:51:33,458
- Oh, boy, how you've grown.

1520
00:51:33,458 --> 00:51:34,927
- [Joel] Yeah, during the
cutaway anything's possible.

1521
00:51:34,927 --> 00:51:38,297
- Keep growing like that, and
you won't fit any clothes.

1522
00:51:38,297 --> 00:51:40,332
Then what are we gonna do?

1523
00:51:40,332 --> 00:51:43,735
- Tommy, come on down
and eat your breakfast.

1524
00:51:43,735 --> 00:51:45,370
- You've gotta hide.

1525
00:51:47,472 --> 00:51:49,007
You understand?

1526
00:51:49,007 --> 00:51:50,475
You've gotta hide.

1527
00:51:51,977 --> 00:51:53,578
- Tommy, did you hear me?

1528
00:51:53,578 --> 00:51:56,280
- [Tom] Can you
feel me near you?

1529
00:51:58,283 --> 00:51:59,650
Oh, what a nightmare.

1530
00:51:59,650 --> 00:52:01,118
Ooh, I dreamt I was
a crappy actress

1531
00:52:01,118 --> 00:52:03,255
in a horrible monster film.

1532
00:52:03,255 --> 00:52:04,823
Hey, wait a minute.

1533
00:52:08,227 --> 00:52:13,097
- [Joel] Oh, no, she really
does have combination skin.

1534
00:52:13,097 --> 00:52:13,932
- [Crow] Ew.

1535
00:52:13,932 --> 00:52:14,765
- [Joel] Oh.

1536
00:52:14,765 --> 00:52:15,633
Oh, my goodness.

1537
00:52:15,633 --> 00:52:16,768
- [Crow] Oh, bad.

1538
00:52:16,768 --> 00:52:17,835
Big bad.

1539
