01:01:32,723 --> 01:01:36,660
- [Tom] Really looked
like a ceiling, didn't it?

1794
01:01:39,163 --> 01:01:40,297
Oh, fun.

1795
01:01:40,297 --> 01:01:41,532
- [Crow] Whew!

1796
01:01:41,532 --> 01:01:42,767
- Tommy, what are you doing?

1797
01:01:42,767 --> 01:01:46,470
- [Joel] It's just my
Spike Jones album, Mom!

1798
01:01:46,470 --> 01:01:47,738
- [Tom] Tommy, now,
you quit warping

1799
01:01:47,738 --> 01:01:50,240
time and space this instant.

1800
01:01:50,240 --> 01:01:51,075
- Tommy.

1801
01:01:52,008 --> 01:01:54,712
Did you hear me, Tommy?

1802
01:01:54,712 --> 01:01:56,047
- Come on, quickly.

1803
01:01:56,047 --> 01:01:57,182
Hide in there.

1804
01:02:00,818 --> 01:02:02,453
- Are you okay?

1805
01:02:02,453 --> 01:02:03,320
- Yes, Mom.

1806
01:02:04,322 --> 01:02:05,188
- What's going on here?

1807
01:02:05,188 --> 01:02:06,223
- Little Joe got out.

1808
01:02:06,223 --> 01:02:07,158
- What?

1809
01:02:07,158 --> 01:02:08,425
- My hamster Joe escaped.

1810
01:02:08,425 --> 01:02:09,893
- Well, try and be a
little more careful.

1811
01:02:09,893 --> 01:02:11,062
I told you a thousand
times, I don't want you--

1812
01:02:11,062 --> 01:02:11,995
- [Tom] I'd like some
breakfast, please.

1813
01:02:11,995 --> 01:02:13,263
- Turning this house into a zoo.

1814
01:02:13,263 --> 01:02:15,265
And stop fidgeting
around like that.

1815
01:02:15,265 --> 01:02:16,467
- Yes, Mommy.

1816
01:02:16,467 --> 01:02:17,368
- All right, now come
downstairs with me

1817
01:02:17,368 --> 01:02:18,535
and behave yourself.

1818
01:02:18,535 --> 01:02:20,638
I've got enough problems.

1819
01:02:22,207 --> 01:02:23,842
- [Tom] Make that
three hard-boiled eggs.

1820
01:02:23,842 --> 01:02:26,677
- [Crow] I've got
to get a series.

1821
01:02:29,213 --> 01:02:31,182
- [Joel] Now, do you think
those are blue contacts,

1822
01:02:31,182 --> 01:02:33,483
or are his eyes
naturally that color?

1823
01:02:33,483 --> 01:02:35,853
- [Tom] Oh, you mean,
like Whoopi Goldberg?

1824
01:02:35,853 --> 01:02:38,188
(Tom laughs)

1825
01:02:39,890 --> 01:02:42,993
Get my head caught
in the snout there.

1826
01:02:42,993 --> 01:02:47,198
- [Crow] Now to find a herd
of cattle to drain dry.

1827
01:02:48,398 --> 01:02:50,835
- [Tom] Meanwhile, in a
winter movie somewhere.

1828
01:02:50,835 --> 01:02:52,737
- [Joel] Gosh, that
last scene was goofy.

1829
01:02:52,737 --> 01:02:55,105
I'm glad we weren't in it.

1830
01:02:55,105 --> 01:02:57,040
- Ah, sometimes there is.

1831
01:02:57,040 --> 01:02:59,010
- I thought hunting wasn't
allowed around here.

1832
01:02:59,010 --> 01:03:00,210
- It's not.

1833
01:03:00,210 --> 01:03:01,378
- Why are you carrying
this rifle, then?

1834
01:03:01,378 --> 01:03:02,880
- [Tom] For you.

1835
01:03:02,880 --> 01:03:04,715
- Well, if that friend of
yours Laura had carried one,

1836
01:03:04,715 --> 01:03:07,050
she'd still be alive.

1837
01:03:07,050 --> 01:03:08,052
- [Joel] Hurts.

1838
01:03:08,052 --> 01:03:09,453
- [Tom] Ooh.

1839
01:03:09,453 --> 01:03:12,923
- [Crow] Hey, it's a
matching shirt and sofa set.

1840
01:03:14,058 --> 01:03:14,892
- [Tom] Hi, gang.

1841
01:03:14,892 --> 01:03:16,693
(Tom humming)

1842
01:03:16,693 --> 01:03:17,795
Hmm, not bad.

1843
01:03:19,230 --> 01:03:21,398
Oh, the new Vogue is here.

1844
01:03:22,900 --> 01:03:24,502
- Molly, is the
television working?

1845
01:03:24,502 --> 01:03:25,970
- I think so, yes.

1846
01:03:25,970 --> 01:03:28,172
- Well, at least we won't
miss "Dallas" this week.

1847
01:03:28,172 --> 01:03:29,640
- [Crow] Oh great,
your friend just died

1848
01:03:29,640 --> 01:03:31,442
and you're gonna watch "Dallas?"

1849
01:03:31,442 --> 01:03:32,877
- [Tom] Shh.

1850
01:03:32,877 --> 01:03:34,912
- Tracy, how can you
kid around like this,

1851
01:03:34,912 --> 01:03:36,780
things being the way they are?

1852
01:03:36,780 --> 01:03:38,015
- [Tom] Thank you.

1853
01:03:38,015 --> 01:03:40,818
- Because if I didn't,
I'd be in hysterics.

1854
01:03:40,818 --> 01:03:41,785
It doesn't work.

1855
01:03:41,785 --> 01:03:42,820
- [Joel] I'm in hysterics!

1856
01:03:42,820 --> 01:03:44,155
- That's strange.

1857
01:03:44,155 --> 01:03:45,857
It was working yesterday.

1858
01:03:45,857 --> 01:03:47,392
- [Joel] I rerouted
the power into Trumpy.

1859
01:03:47,392 --> 01:03:49,093
- The radio makes
a funny noise, too.

1860
01:03:49,093 --> 01:03:50,327
- [Tom] That's called music.

1861
01:03:50,327 --> 01:03:51,662
- Can I go back
to my room, Mommy?

1862
01:03:51,662 --> 01:03:52,863
- Yes, you can.

1863
01:03:52,863 --> 01:03:55,398
- [Crow] For the
rest of your life.

1864
01:03:59,103 --> 01:04:00,170
- [Kathy] How is Sharon?

1865
01:04:00,170 --> 01:04:01,005
- She's gone to bed.

1866
01:04:01,005 --> 01:04:02,105
She was shattered.

1867
01:04:02,105 --> 01:04:03,473
- [Joel] This town's in tatters.

1868
01:04:03,473 --> 01:04:04,742
- [Tom] Shadoobie.

1869
01:04:04,742 --> 01:04:06,977
- So peaceful, so quiet.

1870
01:04:06,977 --> 01:04:08,012
(Tracy chuckles)

1871
01:04:08,012 --> 01:04:10,582
(Tom chuckles)

1872
01:04:13,783 --> 01:04:14,618
- Trumpy.

1873
01:04:16,620 --> 01:04:18,555
(Joel hissing)

1874
01:04:18,555 --> 01:04:20,123
(Tom chuckles)

1875
01:04:20,123 --> 01:04:21,025
- [Tom] Face it, kid.

1876
01:04:21,025 --> 01:04:22,927
Trumpy never loved you.

1877
01:04:26,030 --> 01:04:26,830
Boo!

1878
01:04:26,830 --> 01:04:27,765
Gotcha! (laughs)

1879
01:04:27,765 --> 01:04:29,100
- [Tommy] Trumpy, where are you?

1880
01:04:29,100 --> 01:04:31,902
- [Joel] Were ties
ever that wide?

1881
01:04:34,472 --> 01:04:35,405
- Ah.

1882
01:04:35,405 --> 01:04:36,340
- [Tom] Ah.

1883
01:04:39,377 --> 01:04:40,243
- [Crow] All right.

1884
01:04:40,243 --> 01:04:41,245
S'all right.

1885
01:04:42,580 --> 01:04:43,948
- [Joel] Nothin'.

1886
01:04:43,948 --> 01:04:44,982
- [Crow] Hmm.

1887
01:04:47,852 --> 01:04:48,685
(cat meows)

1888
01:04:48,685 --> 01:04:49,920
- Have you seen Trumpy?

1889
01:04:49,920 --> 01:04:50,922
- [Joel] He tried to eat me.

1890
01:04:50,922 --> 01:04:51,755
He's evil.

1891
01:04:52,890 --> 01:04:54,425
- [Tom] Forget you.

1892
01:04:55,458 --> 01:04:57,362
Boo! (laughs)

1893
01:04:57,362 --> 01:04:59,930
(upbeat music)

1894
01:05:07,137 --> 01:05:08,705
Cujo?

1895
01:05:08,705 --> 01:05:10,073
- [Joel] Evil one?

1896
01:05:10,073 --> 01:05:11,642
- [Joel] Supreme being?

1897
01:05:11,642 --> 01:05:12,543
- [Crow] Alf?

1898
01:05:12,543 --> 01:05:13,510
- [Tom] Chief?

1899
01:05:13,510 --> 01:05:14,945
- [Crow] McCloud?

1900
01:05:15,880 --> 01:05:17,382
- Trumpy, come on.

1901
01:05:18,682 --> 01:05:19,817
Where are you?

1902
01:05:22,753 --> 01:05:23,988
- [Crow] He seeks him here.

1903
01:05:23,988 --> 01:05:25,288
He seeks him there.

1904
01:05:25,288 --> 01:05:27,925
He seeks that rascal everywhere.

1905
01:05:29,760 --> 01:05:31,128
- [Tom] Ah, don't
worry about him.

1906
01:05:31,128 --> 01:05:32,497
He's moody and introspective.

1907
01:05:32,497 --> 01:05:35,967
He's in a corner reading
"Swimming to Cambodia".

1908
01:05:35,967 --> 01:05:36,967
- [Crow] Hmm.

1909
01:05:36,967 --> 01:05:39,270
- Trumpy, are you in here?

1910
01:05:39,270 --> 01:05:42,172
- [Joel] This is, like, the
house of a million foyers.

1911
01:05:42,172 --> 01:05:45,342
(suspenseful music)

1912
01:05:45,342 --> 01:05:46,410
- [Crow] Dad?

1913
01:05:47,412 --> 01:05:48,778
- [Tom] Dum.

1914
01:05:48,778 --> 01:05:49,847
- [Crow] Dad?

1915
01:05:53,583 --> 01:05:56,753
- [Tom] Don't go
into the dining room.

1916
01:05:59,023 --> 01:06:00,557
- [Joel] Here's Tommy!

1917
01:06:00,557 --> 01:06:01,392
- Trumpy.

1918
01:06:05,528 --> 01:06:06,763
- [Joel] Sounds like music from

1919
01:06:06,763 --> 01:06:09,400
the "High Plains
Drifter," doesn't it?

1920
01:06:09,400 --> 01:06:10,835
- [Crow] Yeah.

1921
01:06:10,835 --> 01:06:13,970
- [Tom] Has a Sergio
Leone feel to it.

1922
01:06:15,472 --> 01:06:16,940
- [Crow] Bad choice.

1923
01:06:16,940 --> 01:06:20,477
- [Joel] Oh, those are
ready to pop, I would say.

1924
01:06:24,082 --> 01:06:26,950
- [Tom] Oh, thank goodness
it's summer again.

1925
01:06:26,950 --> 01:06:29,420
We've been driving for months.

1926
01:06:31,188 --> 01:06:33,657
- Doesn't look
like anybody's in.

1927
01:06:33,657 --> 01:06:36,227
- But how can you
tell from here?

1928
01:06:36,227 --> 01:06:38,695
- [Tom] Oh, why don't you
just go up to the door?

1929
01:06:38,695 --> 01:06:41,532
You drove two
seasons to get here.

1930
01:06:42,332 --> 01:06:43,533
For crying out loud.

1931
01:06:43,533 --> 01:06:45,268
- [Crow] Boy, he's
really burning oil.

1932
01:06:45,268 --> 01:06:46,537
- [Tom] Mm-hmm.

1933
01:06:48,372 --> 01:06:52,577
- [Joel] I'm gonna let
this do the talking.

1934
01:06:52,577 --> 01:06:53,743
- Charley?

1935
01:06:53,743 --> 01:06:55,012
Jack?

1936
01:06:55,012 --> 01:06:56,247
Is anyone there?

1937
01:06:56,247 --> 01:06:57,715
- [Joel] He knows 'em,
and he's bringing a gun?

1938
01:06:57,715 --> 01:06:59,250
- [Tom] Oh, it's a
little practical joke.

1939
01:06:59,250 --> 01:07:00,952
He kicks open the door and
plugs them with 30 rounds.

1940
01:07:00,952 --> 01:07:03,187
It's kind of an inside
family thing, you know.

1941
01:07:03,187 --> 01:07:04,422
- [Crow] Housewarming gift.

1942
01:07:04,422 --> 01:07:05,655
- [Tom] Mm-hmm.

1943
01:07:09,025 --> 01:07:09,860
- [Joel] Ah!

1944
01:07:09,860 --> 01:07:10,795
- [Tom] Ooh.

1945
01:07:10,795 --> 01:07:11,962
- [Joel] Oh, it's that guy.

1946
01:07:11,962 --> 01:07:13,497
- What do you think you're--
- Shh.

1947
01:07:13,497 --> 01:07:14,665
- [Joel] Hey, Bill, are those
Haggar slacks you're wearing?

1948
01:07:14,665 --> 01:07:15,465
Farah?

1949
01:07:15,465 --> 01:07:16,700
Dad N' Lad?

1950
01:07:16,700 --> 01:07:18,068
The Guys?

1951
01:07:18,068 --> 01:07:19,470
(Tom chuckling)

1952
01:07:19,470 --> 01:07:20,303
- [Crow] Watch this.

1953
01:07:20,303 --> 01:07:21,305
Little joke.

1954
01:07:22,473 --> 01:07:24,408
Hi, we're the cast
from "Straw Dogs."

1955
01:07:24,408 --> 01:07:27,077
(Crow laughing)

1956
01:07:28,812 --> 01:07:31,048
- [Tom] Sometimes it works.

1957
01:07:32,683 --> 01:07:33,517
Watchtower!

1958
01:07:33,517 --> 01:07:34,518
Oh, just kidding.

1959
01:07:34,518 --> 01:07:35,452
(Tom and Crow chuckle)

1960
01:07:35,452 --> 01:07:36,953
That thing in the magazine.

1961
01:07:36,953 --> 01:07:40,190
- What the hell happened here?

1962
01:07:40,190 --> 01:07:41,225
- [Tom] Hmm.

1963
01:07:42,225 --> 01:07:43,293
- [Joel] Hmm.

1964
01:07:44,295 --> 01:07:45,763
- The radio's not working.

1965
01:07:45,763 --> 01:07:46,763
- [Crow] Oh, nuts, I wanted
to hear Shadoe Stevens.

1966
01:07:46,763 --> 01:07:47,598
- Charley?

1967
01:07:47,598 --> 01:07:48,432
Jack?

1968
01:07:48,432 --> 01:07:49,233
- [Joel] Biff?

1969
01:07:49,233 --> 01:07:50,400
Happy?

1970
01:07:50,400 --> 01:07:51,635
Anybody?

1971
01:07:51,635 --> 01:07:53,470
- You think they're
in the other room?

1972
01:07:53,470 --> 01:07:56,073
- After all this
shouting, I sure hope not.

1973
01:07:56,073 --> 01:07:59,143
- [Joel] Horse poster
compliments Dynamite magazine.

1974
01:07:59,143 --> 01:07:59,977
For teens.

1975
01:08:04,582 --> 01:08:08,118
- [Crow] Turkey legs
in the... (groans)

1976
01:08:08,118 --> 01:08:09,853
- He's dead, I think.

1977
01:08:10,988 --> 01:08:12,757
- [Tom] His last
words were, "Huzzah!"

1978
01:08:12,757 --> 01:08:13,923
- What's that?

1979
01:08:15,358 --> 01:08:17,895
Same mark that Laura had.

1980
01:08:17,895 --> 01:08:19,597
Is he one of the rangers?

1981
01:08:19,597 --> 01:08:21,398
- [Joel] No, but we could
dress him like a ranger.

1982
01:08:21,398 --> 01:08:24,935
- No, he's a poacher,
name of Matt Collins.

1983
01:08:26,737 --> 01:08:29,340
Let's get the hell out of here.

1984
01:08:30,640 --> 01:08:32,275
I don't know.

1985
01:08:32,275 --> 01:08:33,110
- Look out!

1986
01:08:33,110 --> 01:08:33,943
Jesus!

1987
01:08:33,943 --> 01:08:35,312
- [Crow] Ah!

1988
01:08:35,312 --> 01:08:38,248
Alf's back, and this
time it's personal.

1989
01:08:38,248 --> 01:08:41,685
(Tom chuckling)

1990
01:08:41,685 --> 01:08:43,553
- [Tom] Ooh, Reagan's next.

1991
01:08:43,553 --> 01:08:44,688
- [Crow] Pepperidge
Farm remembers!

1992
01:08:44,688 --> 01:08:46,057
Pepperidge Farm remembers!

1993
01:08:46,057 --> 01:08:46,890
The heck with it.

1994
01:08:46,890 --> 01:08:48,025
I'm getting out of here!

1995
01:08:48,025 --> 01:08:49,260
Crackers or no.

1996
01:08:51,895 --> 01:08:54,432
- [Tom] That is the frumpiest
monster I've ever seen.

1997
01:08:54,432 --> 01:08:55,498
- [Joel] Yep.

1998
01:08:57,768 --> 01:08:59,770
- [Crow] Hey, wait,
you got coupons comin'.

1999
01:08:59,770 --> 01:09:02,807
- [Joel] No hitchhikers,
it's company policy.

2000
01:09:02,807 --> 01:09:04,040
- [Tom] Ooh.

2001
01:09:04,040 --> 01:09:05,242
Ah, enough of that
exciting stuff.

2002
01:09:05,242 --> 01:09:08,245
Meanwhile, in still
yet another movie.

2003
01:09:08,245 --> 01:09:10,680
(Crow sighs)

2004
01:09:12,850 --> 01:09:15,818
(Tom hiccups)

2005
01:09:15,818 --> 01:09:17,655
- [Crow] What the?

2006
01:09:17,655 --> 01:09:19,122
- You're a good cook, Tracy.

2007
01:09:19,122 --> 01:09:20,423
Unusual with girls today.

2008
01:09:20,423 --> 01:09:21,892
- Well, my mother taught me.

2009
01:09:21,892 --> 01:09:23,127
She always said
that men like you

2010
01:09:23,127 --> 01:09:25,495
for your meat, and
after your dessert.

2011
01:09:25,495 --> 01:09:26,930
You know how it is.

2012
01:09:26,930 --> 01:09:28,432
If you haven't got a
pretty face to begin with,

2013
01:09:28,432 --> 01:09:29,933
there's nothing you can do.

2014
01:09:29,933 --> 01:09:32,468
- [Joel] Well, I think your
mother had a filthy mouth.

2015
01:09:32,468 --> 01:09:34,905
- Including the
seven-day beauty plan.

2016
01:09:34,905 --> 01:09:36,240
- [Tom] Didn't work.

2017
01:09:36,240 --> 01:09:37,373
- Come on, it's not that bad.

2018
01:09:37,373 --> 01:09:39,042
You've got a lot of good points.

2019
01:09:39,042 --> 01:09:41,278
- Yeah, and I know
the ones men like.

2020
01:09:41,278 --> 01:09:42,813
These and this.

2021
01:09:42,813 --> 01:09:44,315
- But you're very intelligent.

2022
01:09:44,315 --> 01:09:45,448
- Yeah, I don't know what
threatens the guys more,

2023
01:09:45,448 --> 01:09:46,783
my face or my intelligence.

2024
01:09:46,783 --> 01:09:49,687
- [Crow] Yeah, E
equals MC-squared.

2025
01:09:52,288 --> 01:09:54,425
- Hey, I'm getting a bit
worried about Brian and Bill.

2026
01:09:54,425 --> 01:09:55,825
They've been gone now for hours.

2027
01:09:55,825 --> 01:09:57,695
- Oh, maybe they got held up.

2028
01:09:57,695 --> 01:09:59,062
Or couldn't find the rangers.

2029
01:09:59,062 --> 01:10:00,965
- Oh, yeah, these rangers.

2030
01:10:00,965 --> 01:10:01,798
- [Joel] Down, girl.

2031
01:10:01,798 --> 01:10:02,633
Heel.

2032
01:10:02,633 --> 01:10:03,567
Take it easy.

2033
01:10:03,567 --> 01:10:05,135
- All right, Molly, I know.

2034
01:10:05,135 --> 01:10:06,370
Just in case, however,
I'm going to get

2035
01:10:06,370 --> 01:10:07,805
my makeup from the camper.

2036
01:10:07,805 --> 01:10:08,738
I forgot it last night.

2037
01:10:08,738 --> 01:10:09,940
- [Tom] Take a cold shower.

2038
01:10:09,940 --> 01:10:11,208
- Now, what's going on, Tommy?

2039
01:10:11,208 --> 01:10:12,442
You've been running
in and out all day.

2040
01:10:12,442 --> 01:10:13,543
What are you looking for?

2041
01:10:13,543 --> 01:10:14,612
- Nothing.

2042
01:10:14,612 --> 01:10:16,280
Just getting some water for Joe.

2043
01:10:16,280 --> 01:10:17,113
- Oh.

2044
01:10:17,113 --> 01:10:18,348
- Joe?

2045
01:10:18,348 --> 01:10:19,983
Are you hiding a man
somewhere in this house?

2046
01:10:19,983 --> 01:10:21,918
- Joe is Tommy's hamster, Tracy.

2047
01:10:21,918 --> 01:10:23,453
- Oh, what a shame.

2048
01:10:23,453 --> 01:10:27,692
- [Tom] Jeez, Tracy, stay
away from the kid's animals.

2049
01:10:27,692 --> 01:10:30,560
(thunder rumbling)

2050
01:10:31,428 --> 01:10:32,730
(Tom humming)

2051
01:10:32,730 --> 01:10:34,197
(Crow whistles)

2052
01:10:34,197 --> 01:10:37,768
- [Crow] Ba-dump-a-dee,
time to Armor All my pants.

2053
01:10:41,238 --> 01:10:42,472
- [Joel] Oh, this is great.

2054
01:10:42,472 --> 01:10:44,442
He's gonna do that
Bob Newhart routine.

2055
01:10:44,442 --> 01:10:45,275
(Tom chuckles)

2056
01:10:45,275 --> 01:10:46,110
- [Tom] Love that.

2057
01:10:46,110 --> 01:10:46,943
- [Joel] Abner?

2058
01:10:46,943 --> 01:10:47,945
Yeah, hello.

2059
01:10:51,515 --> 01:10:53,183
- Still isn't working.

2060
01:10:53,183 --> 01:10:55,552
Where the hell have Brian
and that old geezer got to?

2061
01:10:55,552 --> 01:10:57,153
It's been seven hours
since they left.

2062
01:10:57,153 --> 01:10:58,688
Didn't have that far to go.

2063
01:10:58,688 --> 01:11:00,357
Maybe something
happened to them.

2064
01:11:00,357 --> 01:11:01,425
- Wouldn't surprise me.

2065
01:11:01,425 --> 01:11:03,127
Bill's as thick as two planks.

2066
01:11:03,127 --> 01:11:04,060
- [Crow] Is he green-treated?

2067
01:11:04,060 --> 01:11:05,428
- How are Sharon and Kathy?

2068
01:11:05,428 --> 01:11:06,863
- They took sleeping
pills and went to bed.

2069
01:11:06,863 --> 01:11:08,665
They were absolutely
scared out of their wits.

2070
01:11:08,665 --> 01:11:10,067
Maybe you should do the same.

2071
01:11:10,067 --> 01:11:13,170
- [Tom] Maybe you
should do the same.

2072
01:11:14,137 --> 01:11:17,007
(thunder rumbling)

2073
01:11:20,577 --> 01:11:21,945
- [Joel] Trumpy?

2074
01:11:21,945 --> 01:11:24,180
I brought you a cup of treacle.

2075
01:11:24,180 --> 01:11:25,015
- Trumpy.

2076
01:11:27,752 --> 01:11:29,453
Where are you hiding?

2077
01:11:31,455 --> 01:11:32,990
- [Crow] Hey, she's
got her L.L. Bean

2078
01:11:32,990 --> 01:11:34,958
disco survival boots on.

2079
01:11:36,727 --> 01:11:38,795
- [Tom] Survive in style.

2080
01:11:40,130 --> 01:11:41,698
- [Joel] Trumpy,
bring me the girl.

2081
01:11:41,698 --> 01:11:43,367
I desire to be read to.

2082
01:11:43,367 --> 01:11:45,868
(tense music)

2083
01:11:47,070 --> 01:11:49,407
- [Tom] Neil Peart on drums.

2084
01:11:50,807 --> 01:11:54,912
- [Crow] Hey, it's Craig
Wasson, all of a sudden.

2085
01:11:58,115 --> 01:11:59,683
- [Joel] Now Trumpy and
I will do my version

2086
01:11:59,683 --> 01:12:01,552
of "Rear Window."

2087
01:12:01,552 --> 01:12:04,120
(woman screams)

2088
01:12:04,120 --> 01:12:05,988
- [Tom] I think
she found Trumpy.

2089
01:12:05,988 --> 01:12:07,825
- [All] Wah, wah, wah.

2090
01:12:10,460 --> 01:12:14,297
- [Crow] Hey, this is not
healthy for a little boy.

2091
01:12:14,297 --> 01:12:15,432
I can't watch.

2092
01:12:19,035 --> 01:12:20,570
- [Joel] Trumpy, no.

2093
01:12:20,570 --> 01:12:21,738
I told you no.

2094
01:12:25,408 --> 01:12:26,243
- Trumpy.

2095
01:12:28,412 --> 01:12:33,383
- [Tom] When good pets do bad
things, on "A Current Affair."

2096
01:12:34,150 --> 01:12:35,418
- [Joel] That was neat.

2097
01:12:36,920 --> 01:12:39,122
(boy gasps)

2098
01:12:39,122 --> 01:12:41,292
Trumpy, we hardly knew ye.

2099
01:12:48,865 --> 01:12:50,133
(Tom coughs)

2100
01:12:50,133 --> 01:12:52,102
- [Tom] Put out the van.

2101
01:12:56,907 --> 01:12:58,808
Oh, so people are being
methodically killed

2102
01:12:58,808 --> 01:13:00,077
by the Banana Splits.

2103
01:13:00,077 --> 01:13:01,245
(gunshot bangs)

2104
01:13:01,245 --> 01:13:02,412
- [Joel] There goes Drooper.

2105
01:13:02,412 --> 01:13:03,247
(gunshot bangs)

2106
01:13:03,247 --> 01:13:04,615
Fleegle.

2107
01:13:04,615 --> 01:13:05,915
- [Tom] Snork.

2108
01:13:05,915 --> 01:13:08,585
(gunshot bangs)

2109
01:13:16,427 --> 01:13:18,428
- Oh, my God.
- Bill.

2110
01:13:18,428 --> 01:13:19,530
- [Bill] So what, she's dead?

2111
01:13:19,530 --> 01:13:21,165
- Yeah, she is.

2112
01:13:21,165 --> 01:13:23,900
What the hell's going on?

2113
01:13:23,900 --> 01:13:24,902
- It was a damned animal.

2114
01:13:24,902 --> 01:13:25,735
- What animal?

2115
01:13:25,735 --> 01:13:26,537
- [Crow] The damned one.

2116
01:13:26,537 --> 01:13:27,370
- Where's Brian?

2117
01:13:27,370 --> 01:13:28,205
- He's dead.

2118
01:13:28,205 --> 01:13:29,205
- Dead, where?

2119
01:13:29,205 --> 01:13:30,740
- Back at the hut.

2120
01:13:30,740 --> 01:13:34,077
- [Crow] Oh, take the
Baretta hat off, old man.

2121
01:13:34,077 --> 01:13:35,878
- [Tom] Aww.

2122
01:13:35,878 --> 01:13:36,880
(Tom chuckles)

2123
01:13:36,880 --> 01:13:39,148
Faster, Trumpy, kill, kill.

2124
01:13:40,817 --> 01:13:41,685
- What the hell?

2125
01:13:41,685 --> 01:13:43,787
What's happening?

2126
01:13:43,787 --> 01:13:45,188
Answer me, you goat.

2127
01:13:45,188 --> 01:13:46,390
What is this?

2128
01:13:46,390 --> 01:13:47,657
What have you done,
you old bastard?

2129
01:13:47,657 --> 01:13:48,592
- Stop it!

2130
01:13:48,592 --> 01:13:49,893
Have you both gone crazy?

2131
01:13:49,893 --> 01:13:52,262
- I want to know who
it was killed Brian,

2132
01:13:52,262 --> 01:13:53,530
and Tracy, and why.

2133
01:13:53,530 --> 01:13:54,363
- I told you.

2134
01:13:54,363 --> 01:13:55,298
- [Tom] We have to go.

2135
01:13:55,298 --> 01:13:56,533
- It was that weird animal.

2136
01:13:56,533 --> 01:13:58,668
And if we stay here,
it'll kill us all.

2137
01:13:58,668 --> 01:13:59,770
- What sort of
fairy tale is this?

2138
01:13:59,770 --> 01:14:00,803
- Oh, listen, Rick.

2139
01:14:00,803 --> 01:14:02,138
We'll sort this out later.

2140
01:14:02,138 --> 01:14:04,908
Now help Bill
carry Tracy inside.

2141
01:14:07,443 --> 01:14:08,278
Bill.

2142
01:14:23,027 --> 01:14:25,162
- You are magic,
aren't you, Trumpy?

2143
01:14:25,162 --> 01:14:27,763
(circus music)

2144
01:14:42,545 --> 01:14:44,413
Trumpy, you come down.

2145
01:14:44,413 --> 01:14:49,385
(Tom shouting)
(circus music)

2146
01:15:02,698 --> 01:15:03,700
I can't bring 'em down.

2147
01:15:03,700 --> 01:15:04,835
I don't know how it works.

2148
01:15:04,835 --> 01:15:07,403
(circus music)

2149
01:15:11,808 --> 01:15:12,675
I'm stuck!

2150
01:15:12,675 --> 01:15:13,510
I'm stuck!

2151
01:15:17,447 --> 01:15:19,717
Oh, we got commercial sign!

2152
01:15:26,923 --> 01:15:29,225
- I really don't know what
kind of animal it was.

2153
01:15:29,225 --> 01:15:30,893
All I know is I was very lucky.

2154
01:15:30,893 --> 01:15:33,130
- Whatever it is, it's
already killed four people,

2155
01:15:33,130 --> 01:15:34,397
and maybe more.

2156
01:15:35,898 --> 01:15:36,733
Where are you going, Rick?

2157
01:15:36,733 --> 01:15:37,667
- To wake up the girls.

2158
01:15:37,667 --> 01:15:38,602
- Why?

2159
01:15:38,602 --> 01:15:40,070
- So we can get outta here.

2160
01:15:40,070 --> 01:15:41,772
I ain't hanging about to find
out who's next for the chop.

2161
01:15:41,772 --> 01:15:42,605
- You can't leave now.

2162
01:15:42,605 --> 01:15:43,473
- No, why not?

2163
01:15:43,473 --> 01:15:44,908
- [Tom] I made quiche.

2164
01:15:44,908 --> 01:15:46,243
- It's getting dark,
'cause the road's blocked,

2165
01:15:46,243 --> 01:15:48,378
because that thing,
that murderous animal

2166
01:15:48,378 --> 01:15:49,613
is maybe waiting for us.

2167
01:15:49,613 --> 01:15:50,847
- [Crow] Yeah, but
give me a good reason.

2168
01:15:50,847 --> 01:15:52,215
- He's right, you know.

2169
01:15:52,215 --> 01:15:54,150
We better wait till morning.

2170
01:15:54,150 --> 01:15:56,387
- Listen, I'm sick and tired
of hearing the same old story.

2171
01:15:56,387 --> 01:15:58,522
- [Joel] I'm sick and tired
of being sick and tired.

2172
01:15:58,522 --> 01:16:00,390
- How can you say that, Rick?

2173
01:16:00,390 --> 01:16:01,625
- Well, I'm getting out of here,

2174
01:16:01,625 --> 01:16:03,393
and if I were you, I'd
take the kid and leave.

2175
01:16:03,393 --> 01:16:04,227
- [Tom] Kid?

2176
01:16:04,227 --> 01:16:05,062
What kid?

2177
01:16:05,062 --> 01:16:05,895
Oh my god!

2178
01:16:06,963 --> 01:16:09,032
- [Crow] Don't start
with me, Martha.

2179
01:16:09,032 --> 01:16:13,070
- If you've got a bit of
sense, then, you'll stay.

2180
01:16:13,070 --> 01:16:14,437
- He's right, Rick.

2181
01:16:14,437 --> 01:16:16,105
He knows the forest.

2182
01:16:17,473 --> 01:16:19,342
- I'd better make sure
that all the doors

2183
01:16:19,342 --> 01:16:21,445
and windows are bolted.

2184
01:16:21,445 --> 01:16:24,447
- [Joel] Now for
some peach cobbler.

2185
01:16:26,617 --> 01:16:29,620
- [Tom] Oh, George,
get me a drink.

2186
01:16:29,620 --> 01:16:31,087
Boo?

2187
01:16:31,087 --> 01:16:32,588
Boo Radley?

2188
01:16:32,588 --> 01:16:33,657
- [Crow] Dark One?

2189
01:16:33,657 --> 01:16:34,758
Beelzebub?

2190
01:16:34,758 --> 01:16:35,592
- [Joel] Chief?

2191
01:16:35,592 --> 01:16:37,060
- [Crow] McCloud?

2192
01:16:38,962 --> 01:16:42,198
Trumpage, Trumpazoid,
the Trumpmonster.

2193
01:16:42,198 --> 01:16:43,233
- [Tom] Trumparino!

2194
01:16:43,233 --> 01:16:45,135
- [Crow] Stretching the premise.

2195
01:16:45,135 --> 01:16:46,202
- [Tom] Yeah.

2196
01:16:50,540 --> 01:16:52,342
- [Joel] He knocked his block
off, but you can press it

2197
01:16:52,342 --> 01:16:55,378
back down again with the Rock
'Em Sock 'Em Robots by Marx.

2198
01:16:55,378 --> 01:16:56,613
- [Tom] So, what can I get ya?

2199
01:16:56,613 --> 01:16:59,717
Ouzo, vodka, Sambuca,
Pernod, Frangelico,

2200
01:16:59,717 --> 01:17:02,218
Blue Curacao, Glenmorangie,
B&B, Hennessy,

2201
01:17:02,218 --> 01:17:04,620
Tanqueray, 100-year-old brandy?

2202
01:17:04,620 --> 01:17:07,157
- I've never needed a
gun to defend myself.

2203
01:17:07,157 --> 01:17:08,725
- Yeah, right.

2204
01:17:08,725 --> 01:17:10,627
You probably pay
others to defend you.

2205
01:17:10,627 --> 01:17:12,495
- [Tom] No, I use a
woman as a shield.

2206
01:17:12,495 --> 01:17:13,563
(gun clicks)

2207
01:17:13,563 --> 01:17:14,798
- What the hell are you doing?

2208
01:17:14,798 --> 01:17:17,900
- [Crow] Beer and a
shot, like you said.

2209
01:17:17,900 --> 01:17:19,402
- [Tom] All right,
all right, I'll get

2210
01:17:19,402 --> 01:17:21,805
the smoky 12-year-old scotch.

2211
01:17:24,675 --> 01:17:26,543
(gunshot bangs)

2212
01:17:26,543 --> 01:17:27,977
- What are you doing?

2213
01:17:27,977 --> 01:17:30,480
- [Joel] He shot my Jim
Beam pheasant decanter!

2214
01:17:30,480 --> 01:17:32,582
- He's gone crazy.

2215
01:17:32,582 --> 01:17:34,685
- Look, what is it with you two?

2216
01:17:34,685 --> 01:17:36,887
Haven't we got enough trouble?

2217
01:17:36,887 --> 01:17:39,455
- I don't like
anyone bugging me.

2218
01:17:39,455 --> 01:17:40,690
(knocking on door)

2219
01:17:40,690 --> 01:17:43,160
- [Tommy] Mommy, open
the door, let me in.

2220
01:17:43,160 --> 01:17:44,427
- It's Tommy.

2221
01:17:44,427 --> 01:17:45,195
- [Tom] I'll get him.

2222
01:17:45,195 --> 01:17:46,697
(imitates gun clicking)

2223
01:17:46,697 --> 01:17:50,500
- [Crow] Tommy, throw open
the door and say "pull."

2224
01:17:50,500 --> 01:17:52,268
- Where did you spring from?

2225
01:17:52,268 --> 01:17:53,737
- [Joel] From your loins, Mommy.

2226
01:17:53,737 --> 01:17:55,105
- Didn't I tell you
to stay in your room?

2227
01:17:55,105 --> 01:17:56,607
- I went to pick some
plants for all the--

2228
01:17:56,607 --> 01:17:58,775
- Plants for all your
animals, I suppose, right?

2229
01:17:58,775 --> 01:18:00,010
That's it.

2230
01:18:00,010 --> 01:18:01,445
Out they're going to
go in the morning.

2231
01:18:01,445 --> 01:18:04,915
Now get to your room and
don't move till I tell you to.

2232
01:18:04,915 --> 01:18:06,683
- Wake up, Kathy.

2233
01:18:06,683 --> 01:18:07,783
- [Tom] I think I got
something to say to you.

2234
01:18:07,783 --> 01:18:08,752
- I heard a shot.
- Shot?

2235
01:18:08,752 --> 01:18:09,753
You must've been dreaming.

2236
01:18:09,753 --> 01:18:11,120
- Wake up!

2237
01:18:11,120 --> 01:18:12,588
- What time is it?

2238
01:18:12,588 --> 01:18:14,323
- [Tom] You know, I'm starting
not to believe this movie.

2239
01:18:14,323 --> 01:18:16,427
I believed it when Alf
went on the killing spree,

2240
01:18:16,427 --> 01:18:17,927
but now I don't know.

2241
01:18:17,927 --> 01:18:19,897
- I don't know, I just hear
voices from downstairs.

2242
01:18:19,897 --> 01:18:22,532
- Wow, those pills
sure are strong.

2243
01:18:22,532 --> 01:18:24,868
I'm gonna take a shower
and try to wake myself up.

2244
01:18:24,868 --> 01:18:27,737
- That's a good idea,
but don't take too long.

2245
01:18:27,737 --> 01:18:29,205
- [Tom] Oh.

2246
01:18:29,205 --> 01:18:32,975
- [Crow] Honey, I'm home,
oh, I'm a little kid.

2247
01:18:35,378 --> 01:18:36,880
- [Joel] Nosy?

2248
01:18:36,880 --> 01:18:38,382
- [Tom] Chirpy?

2249
01:18:38,382 --> 01:18:39,315
- [Crow] Ratboy?

2250
01:18:39,315 --> 01:18:40,417
Sondra Locke?

2251
01:18:40,417 --> 01:18:41,250
- [Tom] Chief?

2252
01:18:41,250 --> 01:18:43,153
- [Crow] McCloud?

2253
01:18:43,153 --> 01:18:45,955
- [Joel] Now, for my wonderful
experiment of joining

2254
01:18:45,955 --> 01:18:49,492
a duck's body to
a rabbit's head.

2255
01:18:49,492 --> 01:18:50,327
There.

2256
01:18:53,330 --> 01:18:55,832
(Tom humming)

2257
01:18:59,302 --> 01:19:01,638
- [Tom] Hey, the
evil one's back.

2258
01:19:01,638 --> 01:19:03,140
- Trumpy.

2259
01:19:03,140 --> 01:19:04,107
- [Crow] Hey, it's like
that scene in "Mac and Me"

2260
01:19:04,107 --> 01:19:05,342
when Mac came back to life.

2261
01:19:05,342 --> 01:19:07,410
- No, stay there.

2262
01:19:07,410 --> 01:19:09,645
Why did you kill that girl?

2263
01:19:09,645 --> 01:19:11,948
Why did you do that?

2264
01:19:11,948 --> 01:19:14,217
Now I can't be your
friend anymore.

2265
01:19:14,217 --> 01:19:15,152
- [Tom] Bad hell beast.

2266
01:19:15,152 --> 01:19:16,887
- [Crow] Did it for the kicks.

2267
01:19:16,887 --> 01:19:18,155
- You're naughty, Trumpy.

2268
01:19:18,155 --> 01:19:19,422
Very naughty.

2269
01:19:19,422 --> 01:19:20,223
- [Joel] Where have
you been, young man?

2270
01:19:20,223 --> 01:19:21,625
This is not a hotel.

2271
01:19:23,193 --> 01:19:25,995
- You wouldn't
kill me, would you?

2272
01:19:28,998 --> 01:19:30,600
Trumpy, was it you?

2273
01:19:32,268 --> 01:19:33,437
- [Tom] I like you, Tommy.

2274
01:19:33,437 --> 01:19:34,637
I'll kill you last.

2275
01:19:34,637 --> 01:19:37,940
- Are you saying
there's another one?

2276
01:19:37,940 --> 01:19:41,478
Listen, Trumpy, Uncle
Bill wants to kill you.

2277
01:19:41,478 --> 01:19:44,313
- [Joel] My advice,
don't let him.

2278
01:19:47,683 --> 01:19:49,585
Looks real bad for you, man.

2279
01:19:49,585 --> 01:19:51,120
- What can we do?

2280
01:19:51,120 --> 01:19:52,322
- [Tom] Oh, you could put
on a play in the backyard.

2281
01:19:52,322 --> 01:19:54,223
Trumpy could play Cyrano.

2282
01:19:54,223 --> 01:19:57,527
- You can't stay here anymore.

2283
01:19:57,527 --> 01:20:00,530
And I don't want you to go.

2284
01:20:00,530 --> 01:20:03,767
Listen, we'll go together
and hide in the woods.

2285
01:20:03,767 --> 01:20:05,268
No, wait here.

2286
01:20:05,268 --> 01:20:07,137
I'll find you a disguise.

2287
01:20:07,137 --> 01:20:08,605
- [Crow] What do you think
he's gonna dress him up as,

2288
01:20:08,605 --> 01:20:09,805
Drew Barrymore?

2289
01:20:09,805 --> 01:20:11,373
- [Joel] Henry Thomas he's not.

2290
01:20:11,373 --> 01:20:12,342
- [Crow] No.

2291
01:20:13,710 --> 01:20:15,145
- [Tom] Oh, suddenly I
feel like someone should be

2292
01:20:15,145 --> 01:20:18,080
reading a Robert Frost poem.

2293
01:20:18,080 --> 01:20:22,952
Something there is that doesn't
love a crummy monster film.

2294
01:20:24,922 --> 01:20:29,092
That's from "Mending Monster
Film" by Robert Frost.

2295
01:20:38,635 --> 01:20:39,937
- [Crow] Neat.

2296
01:20:39,937 --> 01:20:41,872
- [Tom] Mm-hmm.

2297
01:20:41,872 --> 01:20:43,273
- [Crow] Mint julep? (belches)

2298
01:20:43,273 --> 01:20:45,842
- [Tom] No thanks, I've had 12.

2299
01:20:47,210 --> 01:20:50,147
- [Joel] Sure hope
the liquor holds out.

2300
01:20:50,147 --> 01:20:51,882
- [Tom] I don't know.

2301
01:20:57,853 --> 01:20:59,990
(Joel humming)

2302
01:20:59,990 --> 01:21:02,525
♪ I'm in the shower,
nothing will happen to me ♪

2303
01:21:02,525 --> 01:21:03,460
- [Crow] Norman?

2304
01:21:03,460 --> 01:21:04,293
Norman?

2305
01:21:05,262 --> 01:21:06,863
Important phone call.

2306
01:21:06,863 --> 01:21:08,765
- [Tom] I wonder
if Bobby likes me.

2307
01:21:08,765 --> 01:21:09,698
I like him.

2308
01:21:12,702 --> 01:21:15,305
- [Joel] Check it out,
product placement right there.

2309
01:21:15,305 --> 01:21:16,105
Yep.

2310
01:21:16,973 --> 01:21:18,275
(Tom chuckling)

2311
01:21:18,275 --> 01:21:21,143
- [Tom] "Die Hard
2" this is not.

2312
01:21:21,143 --> 01:21:22,478
- [Crow] Hmm.

2313
01:21:22,478 --> 01:21:24,380
Coke, Sprite, Pepto-Bismol,
United Airlines,

2314
01:21:24,380 --> 01:21:25,782
Steve Guttenberg.

2315
01:21:28,552 --> 01:21:29,752
- [Tom] Uh-huh.

2316
01:21:30,953 --> 01:21:32,488
There, now you look
like Admiral Peary

2317
01:21:32,488 --> 01:21:35,358
playing the Elephant Man.

2318
01:21:35,358 --> 01:21:36,693
- Hold on a minute.

2319
01:21:36,693 --> 01:21:38,295
I'll go and investigate.

2320
01:21:38,295 --> 01:21:42,565
- [Joel] Trumpy felt scarred
by his ugly hillbilly nose.

2321
01:21:44,000 --> 01:21:46,870
- [Crow] Looks like a
baseball bat from Alaska.

2322
01:21:46,870 --> 01:21:48,103
- [Tom] Oh, Velvet Hammer?

2323
01:21:48,103 --> 01:21:49,072
Harvey Wallbanger?

2324
01:21:49,072 --> 01:21:50,307
Pink Squirrel?

2325
01:21:50,307 --> 01:21:51,942
Little hair of the
alien that bit ya?

2326
01:21:51,942 --> 01:21:54,510
(Tom chuckles)

2327
01:21:56,112 --> 01:21:57,313
(Crow humming)

2328
01:21:57,313 --> 01:21:58,815
- [Crow] I'm naked and
all alone in the shower.

2329
01:21:58,815 --> 01:22:00,750
I'm totally vulnerable and
somebody could kill me.

2330
01:22:00,750 --> 01:22:02,252
(Crow humming)

2331
01:22:02,252 --> 01:22:03,987
- [Tom] It's probably likely
at this point in the film.

2332
01:22:03,987 --> 01:22:06,388
- [Crow] My brain fell out.

2333
01:22:06,388 --> 01:22:09,625
- [Joel] Say, I
look just like fog.

2334
01:22:09,625 --> 01:22:10,560
- [Tom] Hmm?

2335
01:22:10,560 --> 01:22:11,560
- [Joel] Oh.

2336
01:22:12,728 --> 01:22:16,298
(Crow imitating squeaking)

2337
01:22:18,535 --> 01:22:20,870
- [Crow] You need
a protein rinse.

2338
01:22:20,870 --> 01:22:22,705
And you have dandruff.

2339
01:22:24,007 --> 01:22:24,840
- [Tom] Honey...

2340
01:22:24,840 --> 01:22:25,942
(Kathy screams)

2341
01:22:25,942 --> 01:22:26,777
- [Crow] What?

2342
01:22:26,777 --> 01:22:28,010
What, what?

2343
01:22:28,010 --> 01:22:28,878
What?

2344
01:22:28,878 --> 01:22:31,648
(Kathy screaming)

2345
01:22:33,082 --> 01:22:34,150
- [Tom] Wait, wait, I
made you a special drink.

2346
01:22:34,150 --> 01:22:36,920
Don't forget the coaster!

2347
01:22:36,920 --> 01:22:37,653
- Rick!

2348
01:22:39,222 --> 01:22:40,057
Brian!

2349
01:22:41,190 --> 01:22:42,425
- [Tom] Somebody!

2350
01:22:42,425 --> 01:22:43,693
- [Rick] Kathy!

2351
01:22:44,793 --> 01:22:45,795
(Kathy screams)

2352
01:22:45,795 --> 01:22:47,030
- [Tom] Ooh.

2353
01:22:47,030 --> 01:22:50,233
- [Crow] Don't look
at me without makeup.

2354
01:22:52,135 --> 01:22:52,968
- [Tom] Whoa.

2355
01:22:52,968 --> 01:22:54,370
- [Joel] Oops.

2356
01:22:54,370 --> 01:22:55,372
- [Rick] Open the door!

2357
01:22:55,372 --> 01:22:56,372
- [Crow] But not
with your skull.

2358
01:22:56,372 --> 01:22:57,473
- [Sharon] Molly!

2359
01:22:57,473 --> 01:22:58,342
- What's happened?

2360
01:22:58,342 --> 01:22:59,508
- It's Kathy.

2361
01:22:59,508 --> 01:23:03,112
- [Tom] She's zestfully
dead. (chuckling)

2362
01:23:03,112 --> 01:23:03,947
(gunshot bangs)

2363
01:23:03,947 --> 01:23:05,448
- [Tom] Ow.

2364
01:23:05,448 --> 01:23:07,917
- Quickly, get her onto the bed.

2365
01:23:07,917 --> 01:23:09,152
- [Joel] You know,
this might sound crass,

2366
01:23:09,152 --> 01:23:11,353
but we're getting
really good at this.

2367
01:23:11,353 --> 01:23:12,588
- [Crow] They're gonna
have to build an addition

2368
01:23:12,588 --> 01:23:14,290
just to stack the bodies.

2369
01:23:14,290 --> 01:23:15,558
- What's happening here?

2370
01:23:15,558 --> 01:23:16,358
- [Tom] How big is
a cord of bodies?

2371
01:23:16,358 --> 01:23:17,627
- What was that thing?

2372
01:23:17,627 --> 01:23:18,795
- [Crow] Depends on
how you stack them.

2373
01:23:18,795 --> 01:23:19,728
- [Bill] Some kind
of weird animal.

2374
01:23:19,728 --> 01:23:21,530
- Where are Brian and Tracy?

2375
01:23:21,530 --> 01:23:23,367
- [Joel] What have I done?

2376
01:23:23,367 --> 01:23:24,633
Oh my goodness.

2377
01:23:26,837 --> 01:23:29,172
- Trumpy, what are
you doing here?

2378
01:23:29,172 --> 01:23:30,005
- Go on.

2379
01:23:30,005 --> 01:23:32,308
[Tom] Killing people.

2380
01:23:32,308 --> 01:23:33,242
- Tommy?

2381
01:23:33,242 --> 01:23:34,143
- [Joel] Can you hear me?

2382
01:23:34,143 --> 01:23:35,412
- Tommy!

2383
01:23:35,412 --> 01:23:36,245
- [Joel] Can you
feel me near you?

2384
01:23:36,245 --> 01:23:37,247
- We can't play now.

2385
01:23:37,247 --> 01:23:38,047
Something's happened downstairs.

2386
01:23:38,047 --> 01:23:39,348
You've gotta hide.

2387
01:23:39,348 --> 01:23:41,483
- [Crow] You're my alibi, kid.

2388
01:23:41,483 --> 01:23:42,318
- [Tom] They'll kill you.

2389
01:23:42,318 --> 01:23:44,153
They'll kill you dead.

2390
01:23:46,422 --> 01:23:49,158
- [Joel] This
thing smells musty.

2391
01:23:51,260 --> 01:23:52,428
- Tommy.

2392
01:23:52,428 --> 01:23:54,730
- [Tommy] What is it, Mom?

2393
01:23:54,730 --> 01:23:55,865
- Are you all right, son?

2394
01:23:55,865 --> 01:23:57,200
- Mm-hmm.

2395
01:23:57,200 --> 01:23:58,133
- [Crow] Well,
relatively speaking, yes.

2396
01:23:58,133 --> 01:24:00,237
Depends on what the norm is.

2397
01:24:01,637 --> 01:24:03,305
- Are you sure we ought
to go after it now, Bill?

2398
01:24:03,305 --> 01:24:05,742
- Now's the time to
finish the damn thing off,

2399
01:24:05,742 --> 01:24:06,977
once and for all.

2400
01:24:06,977 --> 01:24:08,612
It's wounded, and we
can follow its trail.

2401
01:24:08,612 --> 01:24:09,845
- Don't go, Rick.

2402
01:24:09,845 --> 01:24:10,647
- Isn't it better to
wait till morning?

2403
01:24:10,647 --> 01:24:11,882
- I tell you, Molly.

2404
01:24:11,882 --> 01:24:13,417
Now is the time
to finish it off.

2405
01:24:13,417 --> 01:24:15,152
- But, Bill, why don't you
leave it for the rangers?

2406
01:24:15,152 --> 01:24:16,085
Isn't it their--

2407
01:24:16,085 --> 01:24:17,353
- Molly, we can't just sit here

2408
01:24:17,353 --> 01:24:19,488
waiting for it to come
back and kill us all.

2409
01:24:19,488 --> 01:24:20,790
- [Tom] Yeah, we
got plenty of booze.

2410
01:24:20,790 --> 01:24:21,723
Let's go ahead.

2411
01:24:21,723 --> 01:24:22,925
- And we gotta do it now.

2412
01:24:22,925 --> 01:24:23,860
- It's not a monster.

2413
01:24:23,860 --> 01:24:25,328
It wants to be our friend.

2414
01:24:25,328 --> 01:24:27,063
- How can you say that
after all that's happened?

2415
01:24:27,063 --> 01:24:28,432
- 'Cause it's true.

2416
01:24:28,432 --> 01:24:31,467
They all wanna be our friends,
but we won't let them.

2417
01:24:31,467 --> 01:24:32,468
- That's enough talking--

2418
01:24:32,468 --> 01:24:33,302
- [Joel] Oh, that's silly.

2419
01:24:33,302 --> 01:24:34,503
Finish your tequila.

2420
01:24:34,503 --> 01:24:35,438
- We'll be careful.
- Don't go.

2421
01:24:35,438 --> 01:24:37,073
There's been enough killing.

2422
01:24:37,073 --> 01:24:38,875
- [Crow] Stop the madness!

2423
01:24:38,875 --> 01:24:40,042
- [Tom] Last call, everybody.

2424
01:24:40,042 --> 01:24:42,512
Finish 'em up.
- You coming or not?

2425
01:24:44,913 --> 01:24:45,848
- [Tom] We'll take a bottle.

2426
01:24:45,848 --> 01:24:48,083
Got a hip flask in the car.

2427
01:24:48,083 --> 01:24:51,387
- [Joel] Hey, he's
mixing his leathers now.

2428
01:24:51,387 --> 01:24:52,955
- [Crow] Wonder
what they wanted?

2429
01:24:52,955 --> 01:24:53,790
Hmm.

2430
01:24:55,292 --> 01:24:56,225
(Tom humming)

2431
01:24:56,225 --> 01:24:57,460
- Sharon!
- Huh?

2432
01:24:57,460 --> 01:24:59,695
- Tommy, both of you,
quickly, come over here!

2433
01:24:59,695 --> 01:25:00,830
Get away from it!

2434
01:25:00,830 --> 01:25:02,165
(Tom chuckling)
- Ooh my god!

2435
01:25:02,165 --> 01:25:04,000
- [Tommy] No, Mommy,
don't shoot him.

2436
01:25:04,000 --> 01:25:05,602
- Tommy!

2437
01:25:05,602 --> 01:25:07,003
- Trumpy is good.

2438
01:25:07,003 --> 01:25:08,538
It wasn't him.

2439
01:25:08,538 --> 01:25:09,772
- [Joel] What he's done is good.

2440
01:25:09,772 --> 01:25:11,473
- Tommy, get away from it!

2441
01:25:11,473 --> 01:25:13,042
- No, Mommy, don't shoot.

2442
01:25:13,042 --> 01:25:14,243
Please.

2443
01:25:14,243 --> 01:25:15,178
- [Tom] Don't make
your mother kill him.

2444
01:25:15,178 --> 01:25:16,678
- Tommy, it's going to kill you!

2445
01:25:16,678 --> 01:25:17,947
- [Crow] I know what
you're thinking, Tommy.

2446
01:25:17,947 --> 01:25:20,850
Did mom fire six
shots or only five?

2447
01:25:20,850 --> 01:25:22,752
- [Molly] Tommy!

2448
01:25:22,752 --> 01:25:25,255
(tense music)

2449
01:25:26,122 --> 01:25:28,792
- [Joel] John Bonham, Moby Dick.

2450
01:25:31,828 --> 01:25:33,395
- Tommy!

2451
01:25:33,395 --> 01:25:35,565
Tommy, come back!

2452
01:25:35,565 --> 01:25:38,100
(upbeat music)

2453
01:25:41,437 --> 01:25:44,373
(tense music)

2454
01:25:44,573 --> 01:25:46,108
- [Joel] John Bonham, Moby Dick.

2455
01:25:46,108 --> 01:25:47,577
- Tommy!

2456
01:25:47,577 --> 01:25:48,845
Tommy, come back!

2457
01:25:48,845 --> 01:25:50,112
- [Tom] Come back, Shane!

2458
01:25:50,112 --> 01:25:51,147
- Come back!

2459
01:25:51,147 --> 01:25:52,082
Tommy!

2460
01:25:52,082 --> 01:25:53,082
- [Crow] Run, Rusty, run.

2461
01:25:53,082 --> 01:25:54,250
- [Tom] Run, Eliza, run.

2462
01:25:54,250 --> 01:25:56,452
- [Joel] You know, that
Trumpy is one ugly--

2463
01:25:56,452 --> 01:25:57,987
- [Crow And Tom] Shut yo' mouth.

2464
01:25:57,987 --> 01:26:00,557
- [Joel] Hey, I'm only talking
about Trumpy, can you dig it?

2465
01:26:00,557 --> 01:26:02,692
- [Bill] We have to cross
over to the other side.

2466
01:26:02,692 --> 01:26:03,927
Let's go.

2467
01:26:03,927 --> 01:26:04,927
- [Tom] Break on through
to the other side, man.

2468
01:26:04,927 --> 01:26:07,063
(Tom laughs)

2469
01:26:07,063 --> 01:26:09,432
- [Crow] Buddy Rich on drums.

2470
01:26:13,168 --> 01:26:16,238
- [Tom] Backed up
by Bill Kreutzmann.

2471
01:26:19,975 --> 01:26:21,810
- [Molly] Tommy!

2472
01:26:21,810 --> 01:26:22,645
Tommy!

2473
01:26:22,645 --> 01:26:24,380
Where are you?

2474
01:26:24,380 --> 01:26:26,448
- [Tom] Fortunately,
Molly was a LLRP in 'Nam

2475
01:26:26,448 --> 01:26:29,118
and knows how to track a
boy with a snout-nosed pal.

2476
01:26:29,118 --> 01:26:31,020
- [Bill] I walked down
stream in the water.

2477
01:26:31,020 --> 01:26:32,022
It's clever.

2478
01:26:36,725 --> 01:26:38,360
- We'll never find him now.

2479
01:26:38,360 --> 01:26:39,195
- Tommy!

2480
01:26:42,732 --> 01:26:44,000
- [Kathy] We must go faster.

2481
01:26:44,000 --> 01:26:45,402
- [Crow] Yeah, yeah,
keep your shirt on.

2482
01:26:45,402 --> 01:26:48,003
I'm wearing a big stuffed suit.

2483
01:26:49,172 --> 01:26:50,907
- [Rick] Not a trace.

2484
01:26:53,677 --> 01:26:54,910
- [Tom] Who?

2485
01:26:54,910 --> 01:26:56,345
- [Rick] We'll have
to wait till daylight.

2486
01:26:56,345 --> 01:26:58,682
- [Crow] Daylight looks
like night anyhow.

2487
01:26:58,682 --> 01:27:00,317
What's it now?

2488
01:27:00,317 --> 01:27:01,517
- [Tom] Day for night, I think.

2489
01:27:01,517 --> 01:27:02,318
- [Crow] Oh.

2490
01:27:02,318 --> 01:27:03,252
Thank you, Truffaut.

2491
01:27:03,252 --> 01:27:04,053
- [Joel] Well, let's go home.

2492
01:27:04,053 --> 01:27:05,722
Our job is done here.

2493
01:27:08,692 --> 01:27:09,958
- [Tommy] Someone's coming.

2494
01:27:09,958 --> 01:27:10,860
Get down.

2495
01:27:10,860 --> 01:27:12,262
- [Crow] Splendor in the grass.

2496
01:27:12,262 --> 01:27:15,398
- [Tom] Grazing in
the grass is a gas.

2497
01:27:15,398 --> 01:27:16,665
- [Joel] Can you dig it?

2498
01:27:16,665 --> 01:27:18,267
- [Crow] High-weed surfin'.

2499
01:27:18,267 --> 01:27:19,135
- [Tommy] Shh.

2500
01:27:19,135 --> 01:27:20,770
- [Tom] Shh!

2501
01:27:20,770 --> 01:27:21,703
Would you--

2502
01:27:21,703 --> 01:27:24,173
- [Tommy] They mustn't find us.

2503
01:27:25,742 --> 01:27:28,177
(Tom coughs)

2504
01:27:29,745 --> 01:27:30,647
- [Tom] Vapor action.

2505
01:27:30,647 --> 01:27:31,480
- Trumpy.

2506
01:27:37,853 --> 01:27:39,488
Trumpy, where are you hiding?

2507
01:27:39,488 --> 01:27:43,425
(whistling theme from "Lassie")

2508
01:27:46,095 --> 01:27:47,297
(Tom coughing)

2509
01:27:47,297 --> 01:27:50,567
- [Tom] Boy, he's gonna
need that gas mask.

2510
01:27:54,970 --> 01:27:56,538
- [Crow] Oh, Trumpy, gross.

2511
01:27:56,538 --> 01:27:58,842
- [Tom] You stepped
in some Trumpy-dumpy.

2512
01:27:58,842 --> 01:28:01,543
- [Joel] You guys, come on.

2513
01:28:01,543 --> 01:28:04,013
(Tommy gasps)

2514
01:28:09,052 --> 01:28:10,687
- [Joel] Whoops. (chuckles)

2515
01:28:10,687 --> 01:28:12,255
- [Tom] I'm gonna
batter fry you, kid.

2516
01:28:12,255 --> 01:28:16,158
- [Crow] Come on,
over the plate, man.

2517
01:28:16,158 --> 01:28:17,360
- Mommy!

2518
01:28:17,360 --> 01:28:18,160
- [Crow] Come on,
rocket it in, man.

2519
01:28:18,160 --> 01:28:18,828
Over the plate, come on.

2520
01:28:18,828 --> 01:28:19,762
- Trumpy!

2521
01:28:19,762 --> 01:28:20,397
- [Tom] Kid, you were set up.

2522
01:28:20,397 --> 01:28:21,230
- Mommy!

2523
01:28:22,732 --> 01:28:23,833
- Sounded like Tommy.

2524
01:28:23,833 --> 01:28:24,600
- [Crow] No, it wasn't.

2525
01:28:24,600 --> 01:28:25,435
It was "Mommy."

2526
01:28:25,435 --> 01:28:26,368
It was an M sound.

2527
01:28:26,368 --> 01:28:28,603
Mmm, like Manhattan, mimosa.

2528
01:28:29,972 --> 01:28:30,773
- Tommy!

2529
01:28:33,710 --> 01:28:36,045
- Tommy, where are you?

2530
01:28:36,045 --> 01:28:37,580
- [Joel] This is,
like, more intense

2531
01:28:37,580 --> 01:28:39,715
than when Bobby Brady got
lost in the Grand Canyon.

2532
01:28:39,715 --> 01:28:41,217
- [Tom] Oh, no,
wasn't that in Hawaii?

2533
01:28:41,217 --> 01:28:43,152
- [Joel] No, that was where
Peter found that Buddha thing.

2534
01:28:43,152 --> 01:28:44,220
- [Crow] Oh, yeah.

2535
01:28:44,220 --> 01:28:45,187
That was cool.
- Oh, yeah.

2536
01:28:45,187 --> 01:28:46,055
- [Tommy] Don't hurt me.

2537
01:28:46,055 --> 01:28:47,590
I'm not like the others.

2538
01:28:47,590 --> 01:28:49,058
(Tom and Joel mewing)

2539
01:28:49,058 --> 01:28:50,527
- [Crow] Ouch.

2540
01:28:50,527 --> 01:28:53,195
(Tom mewing)

2541
01:28:53,195 --> 01:28:56,998
- [Tommy] I just wanna
help you, that's all.

2542
01:28:56,998 --> 01:29:00,637
- [Crow] Stay away from
that, it still hurts.

2543
01:29:00,637 --> 01:29:02,138
- I'm sorry.

2544
01:29:02,138 --> 01:29:03,505
Don't worry.

2545
01:29:03,505 --> 01:29:05,475
I'd just like to help you.

2546
01:29:05,475 --> 01:29:07,610
- [Joel] I conspire
against my own.

2547
01:29:07,610 --> 01:29:10,012
(Tom mewing)

2548
01:29:11,180 --> 01:29:13,482
- I'll blast one,
you take the other.

2549
01:29:13,482 --> 01:29:16,652
- No, please don't hurt them.

2550
01:29:16,652 --> 01:29:18,553
- Get out of the way, Tommy!

2551
01:29:18,553 --> 01:29:19,655
Get out of the way!

2552
01:29:19,655 --> 01:29:21,523
- No, don't hurt them, please.

2553
01:29:21,523 --> 01:29:22,758
- [Tom] Move it, kid.

2554
01:29:22,758 --> 01:29:23,625
I'll have a banana
daiquiri, please.

2555
01:29:23,625 --> 01:29:26,228
(gunshots banging)

2556
01:29:26,228 --> 01:29:27,130
- No, Bill!

2557
01:29:28,397 --> 01:29:30,132
(Bill shouting)

2558
01:29:30,132 --> 01:29:32,635
- [Tom] Long Island iced tea.

2559
01:29:32,635 --> 01:29:34,170
(gunshot bangs)
(creature screams)

2560
01:29:34,170 --> 01:29:37,473
- [Joel] Hey, looks like he
came from the Dumbo planet.

2561
01:29:37,473 --> 01:29:39,475
- [Crow] Time to take the
mask off and see who it is.

2562
01:29:39,475 --> 01:29:41,643
Do you folks at home know?

2563
01:29:45,715 --> 01:29:47,048
- [Molly] Tommy!

2564
01:29:48,217 --> 01:29:51,553
- [Crow] Oh, my ankle,
it's all bendy-wendy.

2565
01:29:51,553 --> 01:29:53,522
- [Sharon] Molly,
we'll find him.

2566
01:29:53,522 --> 01:29:57,860
- [Tom] We may find him
dead, but we will find him.

2567
01:29:57,860 --> 01:30:00,497
- [Joel] Boy, I hope he left
the keys to the liquor cabinet.

2568
01:30:00,497 --> 01:30:01,897
- [Tom] Poor sap.

2569
01:30:03,867 --> 01:30:05,768
- [Crow] Oh,
self-burying monster.

2570
01:30:05,768 --> 01:30:06,835
Explain that.

2571
01:30:09,272 --> 01:30:10,873
- [Tom] Soft beach.

2572
01:30:12,542 --> 01:30:15,110
- [Sharon] Oh. (gasping)

2573
01:30:15,110 --> 01:30:19,482
- [Joel] And he died as he
lived, with his mouth wide open.

2574
01:30:19,482 --> 01:30:20,717
- [Molly] Where's Tommy?

2575
01:30:20,717 --> 01:30:21,517
- He went that way.

2576
01:30:21,517 --> 01:30:22,485
Wait, Molly!

2577
01:30:22,485 --> 01:30:23,285
Come on.

2578
01:30:25,287 --> 01:30:26,822
- Trumpy, I'm sorry.

2579
01:30:26,822 --> 01:30:28,123
- [Molly] Tommy!

2580
01:30:29,292 --> 01:30:30,893
Tommy, answer me, please!

2581
01:30:30,893 --> 01:30:32,895
- [Crow] State it in
the form of a question.

2582
01:30:32,895 --> 01:30:33,863
- [Molly] Tommy!

2583
01:30:33,863 --> 01:30:36,332
- [Tom] Come to the mirror, boy!

2584
01:30:38,868 --> 01:30:39,802
- [Tom] Mm-hmm.

2585
01:30:39,802 --> 01:30:41,270
- [Tommy] It's just no good.

2586
01:30:41,270 --> 01:30:44,073
No, Trumpy, they'll never
let us stay together.

2587
01:30:44,073 --> 01:30:45,542
You frighten them,
you understand?

2588
01:30:45,542 --> 01:30:47,108
- [Tom] For obvious reasons.

2589
01:30:47,108 --> 01:30:48,510
- [Tommy] I'll never
forget you, Trumpy.

2590
01:30:48,510 --> 01:30:50,947
- [Tom] The way you callously
knocked off 15 people.

2591
01:30:50,947 --> 01:30:51,880
I'll never forget that.

2592
01:30:51,880 --> 01:30:53,950
Don't ever change, Trumpy.

2593
01:30:57,118 --> 01:30:58,220
Aww.

2594
01:30:58,220 --> 01:31:00,288
- [Joel] A tender moment.

2595
01:31:01,723 --> 01:31:04,327
- [Tommy] Now please
go and don't come back.

2596
01:31:04,327 --> 01:31:06,295
Do you understand?

2597
01:31:06,295 --> 01:31:08,063
Don't ever come back.

2598
01:31:08,063 --> 01:31:11,367
- [Molly] Tommy, where are you?

2599
01:31:11,367 --> 01:31:12,935
- Go away, Trumpy.

2600
01:31:12,935 --> 01:31:14,037
I hate you.

2601
01:31:14,037 --> 01:31:15,538
Go away.

2602
01:31:15,538 --> 01:31:16,438
- [Joel] Oh, boy, that kid's
really having mood swings.

2603
01:31:16,438 --> 01:31:17,407
- We're not friends anymore.

2604
01:31:17,407 --> 01:31:18,240
- [Joel] That's not good.

2605
01:31:18,240 --> 01:31:19,075
- Go away.

2606
01:31:20,142 --> 01:31:21,243
All right, Trumpy.

2607
01:31:21,243 --> 01:31:22,077
(Tom mewing)

2608
01:31:22,077 --> 01:31:23,178
I'll go, then.

2609
01:31:24,447 --> 01:31:26,148
I'm over here, Mommy!

2610
01:31:26,148 --> 01:31:28,783
- [Crow] Talkin' to Billy Barty.

2611
01:31:30,185 --> 01:31:33,288
(Tom mewing)

2612
01:31:33,288 --> 01:31:35,423
- [Tommy] Mommy, I'm here!

2613
01:31:37,025 --> 01:31:39,828
- [Rick] Molly, he's here.

2614
01:31:39,828 --> 01:31:41,463
- [Joel] No, he's over there.

2615
01:31:41,463 --> 01:31:42,798
- [Molly] Tommy!

2616
01:31:44,967 --> 01:31:46,235
- Mom!

2617
01:31:46,235 --> 01:31:47,637
- [Tom] Sorry, boy,
your uncle's dead,

2618
01:31:47,637 --> 01:31:49,238
but if there's a God
and he tends bar,

2619
01:31:49,238 --> 01:31:51,440
your uncle's bellying
up right about now.

2620
01:31:51,440 --> 01:31:53,142
- Yes, Tommy, all the
monsters are dead.

2621
01:31:53,142 --> 01:31:54,077
Isn't that right?

2622
01:31:54,077 --> 01:31:56,178
(synth music)

2623
01:31:56,178 --> 01:31:57,713
♪ It's been seven ♪

2624
01:31:57,713 --> 01:31:59,548
- [Tom] Oh, nevermind.

2625
01:32:02,818 --> 01:32:04,287
- [Crow] Hey, don't
leave me here.

2626
01:32:04,287 --> 01:32:05,655
I was raised by a child.

2627
01:32:05,655 --> 01:32:08,857
I can't survive
in the wilderness.

2628
01:32:08,857 --> 01:32:10,392
(Tom mewing)

2629
01:32:10,392 --> 01:32:12,495
I'll just wait here, then.

2630
01:32:20,737 --> 01:32:24,307
- [Tom] So. (sighs)

2631
01:32:24,307 --> 01:32:25,407
- [Crow] Hmm.

2632
01:32:26,975 --> 01:32:27,977
- [Tom] Mm-hmm.

2633
01:32:27,977 --> 01:32:32,448
♪ I've laughed with monsters ♪

2634
01:32:32,448 --> 01:32:36,818
♪ I've cried with monsters ♪

2635
01:32:36,818 --> 01:32:41,790
♪ I'll die with
monsters from hell ♪

2636
01:32:42,825 --> 01:32:43,625
- [Crow] I'm
getting out of here.

2637
01:32:43,625 --> 01:32:44,327
This place sucks.

2638
01:32:44,327 --> 01:32:45,060
(Tom chuckles)

2639
01:32:45,060 --> 01:32:46,628
Going back to my planet.

2640
01:32:49,265 --> 01:32:50,667
- [Tom] Hmm, Marine?

2641
01:32:50,667 --> 01:32:51,633
Send in the marines.

2642
01:32:51,633 --> 01:32:52,668
- [Crow] Hey.

2643
01:32:55,437 --> 01:32:57,573
- [Joel] Ah, isn't that
Martin Sheen's son?

2644
01:32:57,573 --> 01:32:58,740
- [Crow] Hey, who isn't?

2645
01:32:58,740 --> 01:33:00,242
- [Joel] Yeah,
got a point there.

2646
01:33:00,242 --> 01:33:01,243
- [Tom] Yep.

2647
01:33:03,812 --> 01:33:06,148
Ooh, that's a good
Italian lunch wine.

2648
01:33:06,148 --> 01:33:07,383
Very light.

2649
01:33:07,383 --> 01:33:10,052
Smooth palate, a
nice woody finish.

2650
01:33:11,587 --> 01:33:14,223
- [Joel] Hey, Martin and
Lewis were in this movie.

2651
01:33:14,223 --> 01:33:15,658
- [Crow] Come on, Jerry,
we've got the rest

2652
01:33:15,658 --> 01:33:16,492
of the credits to get through.

2653
01:33:16,492 --> 01:33:17,727
- [Joel] Wow, Dean.

2654
01:33:17,727 --> 01:33:19,662
- [Crow] Aw, quit
horsing around, boy.

2655
01:33:19,662 --> 01:33:20,930
(Tom sniffs)

2656
01:33:20,930 --> 01:33:24,400
- [Tom] Ah, the fresh
smell of Emanuel Pine.

2657
01:33:24,400 --> 01:33:26,102
- [Crow] Long needle.

2658
01:33:27,970 --> 01:33:29,072
- [Joel] I say
both of those guys

2659
01:33:29,072 --> 01:33:30,538
were in the Knights of Columbus.

2660
01:33:30,538 --> 01:33:32,408
- [Tom] I think they're Two
Guys of the Rotten Union

2661
01:33:32,408 --> 01:33:33,842
is what it is.

2662
01:33:33,842 --> 01:33:35,377
- [Crow] Well, hmm.

2663
01:33:37,713 --> 01:33:40,548
- [Tom] Oh, I thought
I smelled basil.

2664
01:33:40,548 --> 01:33:41,883
Basil!

2665
01:33:41,883 --> 01:33:42,718
- [Crow] Yes, dear.

2666
01:33:42,718 --> 01:33:43,952
I'm doing it, dear.

2667
01:33:43,952 --> 01:33:45,120
How can I do it if
you keep calling me?

2668
01:33:45,120 --> 01:33:46,288
You great cow!

2669
01:33:46,288 --> 01:33:47,723
- [Joel] Come on,
let's get out of here.

2670
01:33:47,723 --> 01:33:48,757
- [Crow] Oh, thank you.

2671
01:33:48,757 --> 01:33:49,792
- [Tom] Chase me.

2672
01:33:49,792 --> 01:33:53,095
- [Crow] Okay. (laughs)

2673
01:34:05,607 --> 01:34:09,978
- Well, guys, looks like it's
time to pack it all in again.

2674
01:34:09,978 --> 01:34:13,082
- Yeah, we are the stuff
dreams are made of.

2675
01:34:13,082 --> 01:34:14,650
- Oh, that's beautiful, Crow.

2676
01:34:14,650 --> 01:34:15,483
Shakespeare?

2677
01:34:15,483 --> 01:34:16,752
- No, Burma-Shave.

2678
01:34:16,752 --> 01:34:18,253
- Oh, well, huh?

2679
01:34:18,253 --> 01:34:21,690
- You know, guys, it always
hurts to close it all up.

2680
01:34:21,690 --> 01:34:22,525
- Yeah.

2681
01:34:22,525 --> 01:34:23,358
- Strike the set.

2682
01:34:23,358 --> 01:34:24,293
- Ow!

2683
01:34:24,293 --> 01:34:26,295
- Wipe off the grease paint.

2684
01:34:26,295 --> 01:34:28,563
Napkin up the blood and entrails

2685
01:34:28,563 --> 01:34:30,665
and move on to another town.

2686
01:34:30,665 --> 01:34:33,035
- Uh-oh, I smell a song.

2687
01:34:33,035 --> 01:34:34,270
- Mm-hmm.

2688
01:34:34,270 --> 01:34:39,208
♪ Tell me, where does
all the magic go ♪

2689
01:34:40,342 --> 01:34:45,247
♪ When the curtain
falls to end the show ♪

2690
01:34:46,148 --> 01:34:49,685
♪ Do the clowns always cry ♪

2691
01:34:49,685 --> 01:34:54,690
♪ When they pack
up the paper sky ♪

2692
01:34:56,292 --> 01:35:01,063
♪ When the champagne
is being poured ♪

2693
01:35:01,063 --> 01:35:06,035
♪ And the lock is on
the old stage door ♪

2694
01:35:07,603 --> 01:35:12,575
♪ Will there still be
a clown in the sky ♪

2695
01:35:13,208 --> 01:35:15,577
♪ For me ♪

2696
01:35:15,577 --> 01:35:18,047
(Tom sobbing)

2697
01:35:19,315 --> 01:35:20,248
- No.
- Don't worry, buddy.

2698
01:35:20,248 --> 01:35:21,750
There'll be other experiments.

2699
01:35:21,750 --> 01:35:22,985
- You really think so, mister?

2700
01:35:22,985 --> 01:35:25,187
- Yeah, take a verse,
it'll cheer you up.

2701
01:35:25,187 --> 01:35:26,822
- Okay.

2702
01:35:26,822 --> 01:35:31,560
♪ When the harlequin
is on the bed ♪

2703
01:35:31,560 --> 01:35:35,932
♪ And the whisky haze
surrounds his head ♪

2704
01:35:35,932 --> 01:35:38,367
♪ William Holden's coming over ♪

2705
01:35:38,367 --> 01:35:39,335
- Tom Servo.

2706
01:35:39,335 --> 01:35:40,535
♪ And he's got a fifth of ♪

2707
01:35:40,535 --> 01:35:42,972
If you don't stop doing
your Anthony Newley,

2708
01:35:42,972 --> 01:35:45,140
I'm gonna throw you
against the wall.

2709
01:35:45,140 --> 01:35:46,408
- He'll do it, too.

2710
01:35:46,408 --> 01:35:50,512
♪ Will there still be
a clown in the sky ♪

2711
01:35:50,512 --> 01:35:51,480
- Help us out, Crow.

2712
01:35:51,480 --> 01:35:55,417
♪ Still be a clown in the sky ♪

2713
01:35:55,417 --> 01:35:57,152
Take it home, Joel.

2714
01:35:57,152 --> 01:36:02,123
♪ Tell me, where is
that clown in the sky ♪

2715
01:36:02,925 --> 01:36:05,760
♪ For me ♪

2716
01:36:05,760 --> 01:36:06,595
(Tom sobbing)

2717
01:36:06,595 --> 01:36:07,530
- I love you, Tom Servo.

2718
01:36:07,530 --> 01:36:08,763
- I love you, Joel.

2719
01:36:08,763 --> 01:36:09,698
- I love you, Crow.

2720
01:36:09,698 --> 01:36:10,900
- You're not my real father.

2721
01:36:10,900 --> 01:36:13,268
- What do you think, sirs?

2722
01:36:13,402 --> 01:36:15,838
- It stinks.

2723
01:36:18,240 --> 01:36:20,810
(solemn music)

2724
01:37:21,270 --> 01:37:22,103
- Well?

2725
01:37:23,438 --> 01:37:24,440
- It stinks.

